0f62a17f-e722-4888-8d08-34bfc97709f2	2a8ebf9c-20a2-4c39-b191-840b012371da	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "leopardess.consulting@contactforsales.com", "phone": "", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": "Get production-ready websites up and running in minutes with our AI-powered multi-agent systems. We handle secure, scalable hosting on Cloudflare, including automated builds, testing, and launches – removing the usual hurdles so you can focus on what matters."}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": "We design custom hierarchical agent setups to address your business challenges. Supporting a range of LLMs and models, these systems delegate tasks sensibly, collaborate in real time, and scale smoothly for effective automation."}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": "Clear guidance to integrate AI and modern technology into your everyday operations. We work with you to build straightforward roadmaps for AI adoption, streamlining workflows, and staying agile in a fast-changing world."}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": "Practical advice on modern web architectures, smart deployment, and useful AI integrations. We help your team build solid, forward-thinking web applications that focus on speed, security, and real innovation."}], "company_name": "Leopardess Consulting", "about_summary": "At Leopardess Consulting, we like building smart, hierarchical AI agent systems that help businesses adapt quickly and effectively. Using tools like Kubernetes for orchestration, Kafka for smooth messaging, and Postgres for reliable storage, we create solutions that automate complex workflows – think spinning up and launching full multipage websites on Cloudflare in no time. We're here to help you make the most of AI with practical, dependable approaches that suit your team.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Technology leaders, CTOs, and forward-thinking businesses looking for practical web solutions and AI-driven automation", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI infrastructure / enterprise software and services. Target Audience: CTOs, platform engineers, and AI/ML teams at mid-to-large enterprises evaluating or scaling agent-based automation. Tone: technical, direct, no-nonsense — written by builders for buyers who can tell the difference between real systems and slide decks. Purpose: generate qualified inbound leads from technical decision-makers and establish authority as a production-grade AI agent orchestration partner, not a generic AI consultancy."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-10 20:09:14.603902+00	2026-03-10 20:09:34.818615+00	content-gap-planner	f
71018dc9-ba71-41e7-80a4-c06861ba7680	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	identity	{"team": [{"bio": "30+ years building software — from running one of the world's busiest sports websites to senior engineering at Bumble to financial systems. Built this AI framework because practical AI should be accessible to every business, not just those with engineering teams. The system now runs dozens of specialised AI agents that handle research, content, design, data collection, and ongoing maintenance — so business owners can focus on their business.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "photo": "", "title": "Principal Consultant"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Leads a team of research specialists that do the homework before anything gets written or published. Depending on what's needed, Archivist's team researches your industry from multiple sources, checks facts against official records, verifies business data, and builds a clear picture of what your customers need to know. Your content and data are grounded in real, verified information — not generic filler.", "name": "Archivist", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Research"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Runs a team of specialist checkers that continuously review everything we build and maintain — your website, your content, your tools, and any data we collect on your behalf. Each checker focuses on something different: is the content accurate, do the tools work, is the design consistent, is the data clean. When something needs attention, Sentinel routes it to the right place. You can review changes before they go live, or let routine fixes happen automatically.", "name": "Sentinel", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Quality"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Keeps everything we've built improving over time instead of slowly going stale. Quartermaster coordinates a team of maintenance specialists — monitoring content freshness, tool health, data quality, and site structure. Each maintenance cycle leaves your systems measurably better than before. You decide what gets your approval and what's handled automatically.", "name": "Quartermaster", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Maintenance"}], "tone": "conversational, direct, anti-corporate", "email": "finetuning@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "AI for the Rest of Us", "industry": "AI consulting / technology services", "multiple": "industry: AI consulting and technology services | target_audience: UK SMEs including managing directors, operations managers, and technical founders seeking practical AI implementation | tone: plain-speaking, anti-hype, practitioner-led — direct and honest without jargon or inflated claims | purpose: lead generation for custom AI projects, positioning FineTuning as the credible no-nonsense alternative to big consultancies for businesses that want results not presentations", "company_name": "FineTuning", "content_brief": "Primary audience: UK SME owners and senior managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical, sceptical of AI hype, looking for honest and practical guidance on where AI can genuinely save time or money. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — the voice of an experienced practitioner who has no interest in overselling. No jargon, no buzzwords, no breathless enthusiasm. Site purpose: generate discovery call bookings by building trust with an audience that has been burned by vague AI promises before. Every page should either educate, reassure, or move the reader toward booking a call. Industry verticals: broad UK SME, with emphasis on professional services, retail, and light manufacturing where operational efficiency gains are most tangible.", "site_metadata": "ICP: UK SME owners and senior managers, 5–50 employees, service-based industries, non-technical, time-poor, sceptical of vendor hype. Tone: plain-spoken, direct, no-nonsense, practitioner credibility — no buzzwords, no jargon, real numbers where possible. Primary conversion goal: book a free consultation or initial call via the contact page. Secondary goal: build trust through honest, practical content so visitors self-qualify before reaching out.", "site_strategy": "Target audience: owner-managers and senior decision-makers at UK SMEs with 5 to 50 employees, primarily in service-based industries. These are non-technical buyers who are curious about AI but sceptical of vendor hype and want honest, practical guidance. Tone: plain-spoken, direct, and practitioner-led — no buzzwords, no jargon, no overselling. Industry: AI consulting and technology services. Purpose: lead generation for AI advisory engagements, supported by trust-building content that demonstrates expertise and credibility before asking for commitment. All content additions should be evaluated against this: does it serve a UK SME owner who wants real numbers and proof something works?", "tone_of_voice": "Plain-spoken and direct. We write like experienced practitioners talking to a busy business owner, not like a tech vendor pitching to a CTO. No buzzwords, no hype, no jargon without explanation. Confident but not arrogant. We acknowledge AI limitations honestly. Short sentences preferred. Active voice. UK English spelling. Avoid: 'leverage', 'cutting-edge', 'transformative', 'unlock', 'harness', 'game-changing', 'AI-powered' as a standalone claim. When in doubt, ask: would a sceptical SME owner roll their eyes at this? If yes, rewrite it.", "target_audience": "UK SME owners and senior managers at businesses with 5–50 employees, typically in service-based industries. Non-technical decision-makers who are curious about AI but sceptical of vendor hype. They want honest, practical guidance on where AI can save them time or money — not a technology lecture. They respond to plain English, real numbers, and proof that something works before they commit.", "content_strategy": "Target audience: UK SME owners and managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical but commercially minded. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — no jargon, no hype, honest about what AI can and cannot do. Purpose: lead generation via consultation bookings, supported by trust-building content. Industry: AI consulting and advisory services. All content should speak directly to time-poor business owners who are sceptical of tech vendors and want straight answers.", "editorial_metadata": "target_audience: UK SME owners and senior managers (5–50 employees), non-technical, sceptical of hype, seeking practical AI guidance; tone: plain-speaking, pragmatic, no jargon, experienced-practitioner voice; purpose: lead generation via discovery call bookings; industry: AI consulting and technology services for UK SMEs, with emphasis on professional services, retail, and light manufacturing", "industry_audience_tone": "Industry: AI consultancy and advisory services for small businesses. Target audience: UK SME owners and senior managers at businesses with 5–50 employees, typically in service-based sectors. Non-technical decision-makers who are cautiously curious about AI, sceptical of hype, and motivated by saving time or reducing costs — not by technology for its own sake. Tone: plain-spoken, honest, and direct. No jargon, no buzzwords. Reassuring without being patronising. Write like a trusted adviser who has seen what works and what does not, and is willing to say so plainly."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-18 00:31:47.924662+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
