c2892476-4ad9-4fac-9e83-89852531bbb0	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	tone_of_voice	{"tone_reference": "Write like a trusted adviser who has seen AI hype come and go and is not impressed by it. Use plain English throughout — if a word sounds like it belongs in a vendor brochure, replace it. Sentences should be short. Paragraphs should be short. Avoid: leverage, unlock, empower, seamless, cutting-edge, transformative, harness, next-generation, robust, scalable, ecosystem, journey. Prefer: save, cut, reduce, replace, automate, check, find, run, build, fix. When explaining technical concepts, lead with the business outcome, not the mechanism. Use real numbers where possible. If something has a downside or a caveat, say so — the audience respects honesty and distrusts anything that sounds too good. The voice is confident but not salesy. It does not oversell and does not hedge everything into uselessness. UK spelling throughout. When writing guides or use-cases pages — where the temptation to drift toward generic AI marketing language is highest — re-read each paragraph and ask: would a sceptical SME owner in Leeds find this useful or would they roll their eyes?"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-18 07:31:30.313095+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
