2659247d-6217-49f4-9f23-c336eff4b2ca	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "leopardess@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": ""}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": ""}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": ""}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": ""}], "company_name": "Leopardess Consulting", "about_summary": "At Leopardess Consulting, we like building smart, hierarchical AI agent systems that help businesses adapt quickly and effectively. Using tools like Kubernetes for orchestration, Kafka for smooth messaging, and Postgres for reliable storage, we create solutions that automate complex workflows – think spinning up and launching full multipage websites on Cloudflare in no time. We're here to help you make the most of AI with practical, dependable approaches that suit your team.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Three primary personas: (1) CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who are under pressure to ship AI capabilities fast, have existing cloud infrastructure, and are sceptical of consultancies that can't show working code — they want proof of production deployments, not decks. (2) Founders of B2B SaaS or professional services companies who are technically literate but lack an internal AI/ML team, are evaluating whether to build or buy agent orchestration, and need a trusted partner who can own delivery end-to-end. (3) Operations or transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses who have identified repetitive, high-volume workflows (reporting, data ingestion, client onboarding) and need a practical path to automation without hiring a full data engineering team. All three are time-poor, results-driven, and respond to specificity, working demos, and clear ROI framing over abstract capability claims.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "brand_voice_guidelines": "The Leopardess name is a live brand asset and should be referenced naturally at least once per page through metaphor rather than explicit explanation. The leopardess archetype carries: speed (fast delivery, rapid iteration, no slow consulting cycles), precision (targeted solutions, no wasted motion, surgical automation), adaptability (hunts in complex terrain, works across stacks and sectors), and instinct (pattern recognition, knowing where to move before the client does). Apply these qualities to describe how the team works, how systems are built, and how problems are approached. Examples: 'We move fast because we've already mapped the terrain', 'precision-built agents, not broad-brush automation', 'we don't advise from the sidelines — we hunt the problem alongside you'. Avoid forced or literal animal references. The metaphor should feel like a natural extension of the practical-expert voice, not a mascot gimmick.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration / technology services. Target Audience: CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments; founders of B2B SaaS or professional services companies evaluating build-vs-buy for agent orchestration; operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses automating high-volume workflows. Tone: Direct, technically credible, evidence-led — the voice of practitioners who ship working systems, not consultants who produce decks. Purpose: Lead generation and service conversion, achieved by demonstrating technical depth, showing real production deployments, and giving time-poor technical buyers enough specificity to self-qualify and initiate contact."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-13 14:23:21.748032+00	2026-03-14 13:22:40.724303+00	content-gap-planner	f
