8f76614d-d3dc-410f-9b44-18f25f3ea66f	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	identity	{"tone": "conversational, direct, anti-corporate", "email": "finetuning@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "AI for the Rest of Us", "industry": "AI consulting / technology services", "multiple": "industry: AI consulting and technology services | target_audience: UK SMEs including managing directors, operations managers, and technical founders seeking practical AI implementation | tone: plain-speaking, anti-hype, practitioner-led — direct and honest without jargon or inflated claims | purpose: lead generation for custom AI projects, positioning FineTuning as the credible no-nonsense alternative to big consultancies for businesses that want results not presentations", "company_name": "FineTuning", "tone_of_voice": "Plain-spoken and direct. We write like experienced practitioners talking to a busy business owner, not like a tech vendor pitching to a CTO. No buzzwords, no hype, no jargon without explanation. Confident but not arrogant. We acknowledge AI limitations honestly. Short sentences preferred. Active voice. UK English spelling. Avoid: 'leverage', 'cutting-edge', 'transformative', 'unlock', 'harness', 'game-changing', 'AI-powered' as a standalone claim. When in doubt, ask: would a sceptical SME owner roll their eyes at this? If yes, rewrite it.", "target_audience": "UK SME owners and senior managers with 5–50 employees, typically non-technical, who are curious about AI but sceptical of hype. They want honest, practical advice on where AI can genuinely save time or money in their business — not a technology lecture. Primary conversion goal is to book a discovery call. Industry verticals are broad but may skew toward professional services, retail, and light manufacturing where operational efficiency gains are most tangible.", "content_strategy": "Target audience: UK SME owners and managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical but commercially minded. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — no jargon, no hype, honest about what AI can and cannot do. Purpose: lead generation via consultation bookings, supported by trust-building content. Industry: AI consulting and advisory services. All content should speak directly to time-poor business owners who are sceptical of tech vendors and want straight answers."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 12:33:05.33137+00	2026-03-14 13:41:37.597697+00	content-gap-planner	f
3c589eba-960d-4d35-a135-11d5d562ca13	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	site_plan	{"response": {"pages": [{"name": "index", "title": "FineTuning | AI Systems That Actually Work", "sections": ["hero", "differentiators-section", "services-grid", "social_proof", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Home", "nav_order": 1}, {"name": "services", "title": "Services | FineTuning", "sections": ["services-hero", "services-grid", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Services", "nav_order": 2}, {"name": "approach", "title": "Our Approach | FineTuning", "sections": ["hero", "features", "differentiators-section", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Approach", "nav_order": 3}, {"name": "use-cases", "title": "Use Cases | FineTuning", "sections": ["use-cases-hero", "use-cases-list", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Use Cases", "nav_order": 4}, {"name": "about", "title": "About Us | FineTuning", "sections": ["about-hero", "about-content", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "About", "nav_order": 5}, {"name": "contact", "title": "Contact Us | FineTuning", "sections": ["contact-hero", "contact-form", "contact-info"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Contact", "nav_order": 6}], "needs_logo": true, "needs_images": true, "image_prompts": {"logo": "A modern, technical logo for an AI systems company called FineTuning. Use clean, precise geometric shapes suggesting neural networks or data pipelines with a professional color palette of deep navy blue and electric blue accents. The design should convey technical expertise, precision, and practical engineering rather than flashy AI marketing.", "hero_home": "A sophisticated, technical background featuring abstract representations of interconnected systems and data flows. Use a dark professional palette with deep navy blues and subtle electric blue highlights. Include geometric patterns suggesting neural networks, automation pipelines, and distributed agent systems. The mood should be serious, technical, and focused on real engineering rather than AI hype."}, "style_collection": "professional-dark"}, "response_status": "complete", "response_received_at": "2026-03-18T13:06:03Z"}	pageflow-builder	site-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-18 13:06:18.425578+00	2026-03-18 13:32:31.155525+00	site-planner	f
e8afe721-056d-4e85-bb5e-6f0d0da0d0d6	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	briefing	{"tagline": "From idea to AI system", "about_us": "  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our aim is to make AI genuinely useful.   ## AI systems that actually do the work  Most companies experimenting with AI end up with prototypes, demos, or chatbots.  Very few end up with systems that **save time, automate work, or generate measurable value**.  Finetune helps organisations design and deploy practical AI systems — automation pipelines, specialised models, and intelligent agents that solve real operational problems.  Not AI theatre.  ---  Real systems.  # Rapid experimentation  AI technology is moving quickly.  The companies that benefit most are those that can **experiment cheaply and deploy quickly**.  We aim to make it easy to test ideas, build prototypes, and evolve them into real systems when they prove useful.   ---  # What we build  We work with companies to build AI infrastructure that fits into real workflows.  ### Automation systems  AI that screens requests, processes documents, extracts information, and routes work automatically.  ### Intelligent agent pipelines  Systems where multiple AI agents collaborate to solve problems, analyse information, or complete complex tasks.  ### Custom AI models  Fine-tuned models trained on domain-specific data using techniques such as LoRA and other efficient training methods.  ### RAG systems for company knowledge  AI that can search and reason over internal data such as documents, emails, financial information, and knowledge bases.  ### Private AI deployments  Secure systems where models can run locally or within controlled environments to protect sensitive data.  ### Data collection infrastructure  Large-scale web data pipelines capable of gathering structured information from thousands of sources.  ---  # Why most AI projects fail  Many AI initiatives stall for predictable reasons.  **They start with tools instead of problems.**  **They stay in prototype mode.**  **They rely on third-party systems that can’t integrate with existing workflows.**  **Or they assume a single AI model will magically solve everything.**  In practice, useful AI systems usually require:  * data pipelines * automation layers * model adaptation * monitoring and iteration  AI works best as **part of a system**, not as a standalone tool.  ---  # The Finetune approach  We focus on **practical deployment**.  That means starting with a real operational problem and designing a system around it.  A typical project might involve:  1. Collecting and structuring the relevant data 2. Building automation pipelines 3. Training or adapting models 4. Integrating the system into existing workflows 5. Iterating until the system reliably saves time or improves decisions  The goal is not simply to use AI.  The goal is to make something **genuinely useful**.  ---  # What we can help with  Examples of problems we help solve:  * Screening and routing incoming requests * Automating quoting or proposal workflows * Extracting structured information from documents * Building internal knowledge assistants * Collecting market or financial data at scale * Deploying private AI models for sensitive workflows * Setting up agent pipelines that can perform complex multi-step tasks  Some systems are simple and highly targeted.  Others involve networks of cooperating agents and large-scale data pipelines.  ---  # A note on scale  We are particularly interested in **agent systems and large-scale automation**.  This includes experimentation with environments where thousands of AI agents can communicate and collaborate to solve problems.  These systems are still emerging, but they point toward a future where much of the routine work inside organisations can be handled by coordinated software agents.  Our goal is to help companies begin exploring that future in a practical way.  ---    ---  # Who we work with  We tend to work best with organisations that:  * have complex workflows or data * are open to experimentation * want to build internal capability with AI rather than just outsource it  This includes startups, established companies, and technical teams exploring new ways to operate.  ---  # About Finetune  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our focus is simple:  **make AI genuinely useful inside real organisations.**  ---  # Call to action  ## Curious what AI could automate in your business?  We’re always happy to have a technical conversation about possible approaches.  Contact us to discuss your workflows, data, or ideas.", "services": [{"name": "AI Automation Systems  ", "description": "Design and deployment of AI-driven automation pipelines that remove manual work from business processes. Examples include request screening, automated quoting, document analysis, and workflow orchestration."}, {"name": "Intelligent Agent Systems", "description": "Design and deployment of networks of AI agents capable of solving complex tasks collaboratively. These systems can analyse information, communicate with each other, and perform large-scale problem solving. Talk to us about systems capable of running tens of thousands of AI agents communicating with each other to solve complex tasks."}, {"name": "Custom AI Model Training", "description": "Training specialised models using techniques such as LoRA, DoRA, and other parameter-efficient methods to adapt modern AI models to your company's specific needs."}, {"name": "RAG Systems for Company Data", "description": "Deployment of Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems that allow AI to search and reason over your internal data including:  Emails  Documents  Financial records  Marketing material  Knowledge bases"}, {"name": "Bulk Data Collection", "description": "Large-scale web data extraction across thousands of websites, including structured business and financial data collection."}, {"name": "Financial and Company Data Pipelines", "description": "Automated systems for collecting and analysing financial data from public sources including company registries and regulatory filings."}, {"name": "Private AI Deployments", "description": "Secure deployment of AI systems that run privately — including models that can run locally or in-browser to protect company data and reduce usage costs."}, {"name": "Agent Pipeline Infrastructure", "description": "Installation and configuration of agent frameworks and orchestration systems so companies can run their own AI agents in production."}, {"name": "Rapid Website Generation", "description": "Creation of complex, high-quality static websites within minutes for:  company identity  marketing pages  landing pages  documentation  presentations"}, {"name": "AI Strategy & Implementation", "description": "Hands-on support helping companies move from curiosity about AI to systems that actually work inside their business."}, {"name": "High-Volume Data Acquisition", "description": "Design systems capable of collecting structured information from thousands of websites automatically."}], "company_name": "FineTuning"}	pageflow-builder	briefing-agent	\N	\N	f	2026-03-18 13:32:21.504547+00	2026-03-18 14:15:45.730262+00	briefing-agent	f
b31676c9-4c03-4294-8cb9-7c55a10ad151	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	messaging	{"speed_claim_canonical": "Use a single, consistent, defensible speed claim across all pages. Recommended phrasing: 'in hours, not weeks' — this is credible to technical audiences, avoids the implausibility of 'minutes' for production-grade AI agent work, and still communicates meaningful speed advantage. Retire both 'in minutes—not weeks' and 'in minutes, not months'. If a 'minutes' claim is retained for a specific narrow use case (e.g. a demo or a specific automated report generation feature), scope it explicitly to that feature rather than using it as a general company-wide claim. Audit all pages including index, about, services, use-cases, and any insight articles for instances of the speed claim and update to the canonical version."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-19 14:37:34.872559+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
1ab1f10f-80f1-4abe-89cf-04e9be69b0dc	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "leopardess@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": ""}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": ""}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": ""}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": ""}], "site_brief": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration (technology services). Primary audience: Three personas — (1) CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments and working code, not slide decks; (2) Founders of B2B SaaS or professional services firms who are technically literate, lack an internal AI/ML team, and need a delivery partner who can own end-to-end build; (3) Operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses seeking practical automation of high-volume workflows without hiring a full data engineering team. All three personas are time-poor, results-driven, and respond to specificity, working demos, and clear ROI framing. Tone: Practical, direct, technically credible — the voice of engineers who build real systems, not consultants who produce reports. Conversion purpose: Generate qualified inbound leads and demo requests from UK businesses ready to commission AI agent or automation work, with a secondary goal of establishing technical authority through case studies, tools, and insights content.", "company_name": "Leopardess Consulting", "about_summary": "At Leopardess Consulting, we like building smart, hierarchical AI agent systems that help businesses adapt quickly and effectively. Using tools like Kubernetes for orchestration, Kafka for smooth messaging, and Postgres for reliable storage, we create solutions that automate complex workflows – think spinning up and launching full multipage websites on Cloudflare in no time. We're here to help you make the most of AI with practical, dependable approaches that suit your team.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "CTOs, engineering leads, and technical founders at UK scale-ups and B2B SaaS companies who evaluate vendors on production credibility, stack depth, and delivery track record. Secondary audience includes technically-literate business decision-makers who can assess system architecture and engineering quality. Non-technical SMB buyers are explicitly out of scope.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "brand_voice_guidelines": "The Leopardess name is a live brand asset and should be referenced naturally at least once per page through metaphor rather than explicit explanation. The leopardess archetype carries: speed (fast delivery, rapid iteration, no slow consulting cycles), precision (targeted solutions, no wasted motion, surgical automation), adaptability (hunts in complex terrain, works across stacks and sectors), and instinct (pattern recognition, knowing where to move before the client does). Apply these qualities to describe how the team works, how systems are built, and how problems are approached. Examples: 'We move fast because we've already mapped the terrain', 'precision-built agents, not broad-brush automation', 'we don't advise from the sidelines — we hunt the problem alongside you'. Avoid forced or literal animal references. The metaphor should feel like a natural extension of the practical-expert voice, not a mascot gimmick.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration / technology services. Target Audience: CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments; founders of B2B SaaS or professional services companies evaluating build-vs-buy for agent orchestration; operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses automating high-volume workflows. Tone: Direct, technically credible, evidence-led — the voice of practitioners who ship working systems, not consultants who produce decks. Purpose: Lead generation and service conversion, achieved by demonstrating technical depth, showing real production deployments, and giving time-poor technical buyers enough specificity to self-qualify and initiate contact."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 15:38:54.762965+00	2026-03-14 15:40:36.168854+00	content-gap-planner	f
