7dc330ca-bde3-4cd7-80e6-dbf3aa2b5fbf	5fe15466-4e2e-4ff2-981e-98c1b7074002	identity	{"email": "gas@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "contact": {"email": null, "phone": null, "address": null, "location": null}, "tagline": null, "industry": "Energy & Fuel Distribution", "services": [{"name": "Wholesale Fuel Distribution", "description": "Bulk supply of gasoline and diesel to retailers and commercial clients"}, {"name": "Fleet Fuel Services", "description": "Fuel supply solutions for commercial fleet operations"}, {"name": "Natural Gas Distribution", "description": "Wholesale natural gas supply to industrial and commercial customers"}, {"name": "Rack Pricing Programs", "description": "Wholesale rack fuel pricing for resellers and distributors"}], "key_people": [], "company_name": "Gas Wholesalers", "sub_industry": "Wholesale Gas & Petroleum Products", "about_summary": "Gas Wholesalers appears to be a wholesale distribution company focused on gas and petroleum products. Based on the domain name and industry research, this likely involves the wholesale supply of gasoline, diesel, natural gas, or related energy products to retailers, fleet operators, or industrial clients. The company would operate in the B2B fuel distribution market.", "site_strategy": "Industry: Petroleum wholesale and fuel distribution. Target audience: Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases. Tone: Direct, professional, no-nonsense — written from the perspective of experienced industry insiders, not salespeople. Emphasis on reliability, pricing transparency, and straightforward service. Purpose: Generate qualified B2B leads from fuel buyers who need a dependable wholesale distribution partner.", "social_profiles": {}, "target_audience": "Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases", "competitors_found": ["econogas.ca", "igasusa.com"], "has_existing_site": false, "existing_site_quality": "none", "unique_selling_points": ["Wholesale pricing for bulk fuel purchases", "Direct terminal access and distribution networks", "B2B focused fuel supply solutions", "Competitive rack pricing programs"], "tagline_and_product_terminology": "Replace the current tagline 'Wholesale Gas Supply Solutions' with one that reflects the full product scope, such as 'Wholesale Fuel, Natural Gas & Specialty Gas Distribution' or 'Complete Wholesale Fuel & Gas Supply.' Define three canonical product categories for use across all pages: (1) Wholesale Fuel Distribution — gasoline, diesel, and refined petroleum products; (2) Natural Gas Distribution — commercial and industrial natural gas supply; (3) Specialty Gases — any non-commodity gas products referenced on the services page. Enforce this terminology framework site-wide so homepage subheadlines, service descriptions, page titles, and meta descriptions all use the same category names without variation.", "industry, target_audience, tone, purpose": "industry: 'wholesale fuel distribution'; target_audience: 'fuel retailers, fleet operators, commercial and industrial buyers'; tone: 'direct and professional'; purpose: 'generate qualified inbound leads for bulk fuel supply contracts'"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 14:17:41.483486+00	2026-03-14 21:43:16.501559+00	content-gap-planner	f
f6a72a2f-f12b-4b7a-942b-2f8f1b90c8c8	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	briefing	{"tagline": "From idea to AI system", "about_us": "  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our aim is to make AI genuinely useful.   ## AI systems that actually do the work  Most companies experimenting with AI end up with prototypes, demos, or chatbots.  Very few end up with systems that **save time, automate work, or generate measurable value**.  Finetune helps organisations design and deploy practical AI systems — automation pipelines, specialised models, and intelligent agents that solve real operational problems.  Not AI theatre.  ---  Real systems.  # Rapid experimentation  AI technology is moving quickly.  The companies that benefit most are those that can **experiment cheaply and deploy quickly**.  We aim to make it easy to test ideas, build prototypes, and evolve them into real systems when they prove useful.   ---  # What we build  We work with companies to build AI infrastructure that fits into real workflows.  ### Automation systems  AI that screens requests, processes documents, extracts information, and routes work automatically.  ### Intelligent agent pipelines  Systems where multiple AI agents collaborate to solve problems, analyse information, or complete complex tasks.  ### Custom AI models  Fine-tuned models trained on domain-specific data using techniques such as LoRA and other efficient training methods.  ### RAG systems for company knowledge  AI that can search and reason over internal data such as documents, emails, financial information, and knowledge bases.  ### Private AI deployments  Secure systems where models can run locally or within controlled environments to protect sensitive data.  ### Data collection infrastructure  Large-scale web data pipelines capable of gathering structured information from thousands of sources.  ---  # Why most AI projects fail  Many AI initiatives stall for predictable reasons.  **They start with tools instead of problems.**  **They stay in prototype mode.**  **They rely on third-party systems that can’t integrate with existing workflows.**  **Or they assume a single AI model will magically solve everything.**  In practice, useful AI systems usually require:  * data pipelines * automation layers * model adaptation * monitoring and iteration  AI works best as **part of a system**, not as a standalone tool.  ---  # The Finetune approach  We focus on **practical deployment**.  That means starting with a real operational problem and designing a system around it.  A typical project might involve:  1. Collecting and structuring the relevant data 2. Building automation pipelines 3. Training or adapting models 4. Integrating the system into existing workflows 5. Iterating until the system reliably saves time or improves decisions  The goal is not simply to use AI.  The goal is to make something **genuinely useful**.  ---  # What we can help with  Examples of problems we help solve:  * Screening and routing incoming requests * Automating quoting or proposal workflows * Extracting structured information from documents * Building internal knowledge assistants * Collecting market or financial data at scale * Deploying private AI models for sensitive workflows * Setting up agent pipelines that can perform complex multi-step tasks  Some systems are simple and highly targeted.  Others involve networks of cooperating agents and large-scale data pipelines.  ---  # A note on scale  We are particularly interested in **agent systems and large-scale automation**.  This includes experimentation with environments where thousands of AI agents can communicate and collaborate to solve problems.  These systems are still emerging, but they point toward a future where much of the routine work inside organisations can be handled by coordinated software agents.  Our goal is to help companies begin exploring that future in a practical way.  ---    ---  # Who we work with  We tend to work best with organisations that:  * have complex workflows or data * are open to experimentation * want to build internal capability with AI rather than just outsource it  This includes startups, established companies, and technical teams exploring new ways to operate.  ---  # About Finetune  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our focus is simple:  **make AI genuinely useful inside real organisations.**  ---  # Call to action  ## Curious what AI could automate in your business?  We’re always happy to have a technical conversation about possible approaches.  Contact us to discuss your workflows, data, or ideas.", "services": [{"name": "AI Automation Systems  ", "description": "Design and deployment of AI-driven automation pipelines that remove manual work from business processes. Examples include request screening, automated quoting, document analysis, and workflow orchestration."}, {"name": "Intelligent Agent Systems", "description": "Design and deployment of networks of AI agents capable of solving complex tasks collaboratively. These systems can analyse information, communicate with each other, and perform large-scale problem solving. Talk to us about systems capable of running tens of thousands of AI agents communicating with each other to solve complex tasks."}, {"name": "Custom AI Model Training", "description": "Training specialised models using techniques such as LoRA, DoRA, and other parameter-efficient methods to adapt modern AI models to your company's specific needs."}, {"name": "RAG Systems for Company Data", "description": "Deployment of Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems that allow AI to search and reason over your internal data including:  Emails  Documents  Financial records  Marketing material  Knowledge bases"}, {"name": "Bulk Data Collection", "description": "Large-scale web data extraction across thousands of websites, including structured business and financial data collection."}, {"name": "Financial and Company Data Pipelines", "description": "Automated systems for collecting and analysing financial data from public sources including company registries and regulatory filings."}, {"name": "Private AI Deployments", "description": "Secure deployment of AI systems that run privately — including models that can run locally or in-browser to protect company data and reduce usage costs."}, {"name": "Agent Pipeline Infrastructure", "description": "Installation and configuration of agent frameworks and orchestration systems so companies can run their own AI agents in production."}, {"name": "Rapid Website Generation", "description": "Creation of complex, high-quality static websites within minutes for:  company identity  marketing pages  landing pages  documentation  presentations"}, {"name": "AI Strategy & Implementation", "description": "Hands-on support helping companies move from curiosity about AI to systems that actually work inside their business."}, {"name": "High-Volume Data Acquisition", "description": "Design systems capable of collecting structured information from thousands of websites automatically."}], "company_name": "FineTuning"}	pageflow-builder	briefing-agent	\N	\N	f	2026-03-20 13:49:00.003345+00	2026-03-21 11:15:23.039018+00	briefing-agent	f
fbf35d07-ae39-4091-bb17-39e906e8f17d	5fe15466-4e2e-4ff2-981e-98c1b7074002	identity	{"email": "gas@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "contact": {"email": null, "phone": null, "address": null, "location": null}, "tagline": null, "industry": "Energy & Fuel Distribution", "services": [{"name": "Wholesale Fuel Distribution", "description": "Bulk supply of gasoline and diesel to retailers and commercial clients"}, {"name": "Fleet Fuel Services", "description": "Fuel supply solutions for commercial fleet operations"}, {"name": "Natural Gas Distribution", "description": "Wholesale natural gas supply to industrial and commercial customers"}, {"name": "Rack Pricing Programs", "description": "Wholesale rack fuel pricing for resellers and distributors"}], "key_people": [], "company_name": "Gas Wholesalers", "sub_industry": "Wholesale Gas & Petroleum Products", "about_summary": "Gas Wholesalers appears to be a wholesale distribution company focused on gas and petroleum products. Based on the domain name and industry research, this likely involves the wholesale supply of gasoline, diesel, natural gas, or related energy products to retailers, fleet operators, or industrial clients. The company would operate in the B2B fuel distribution market.", "site_strategy": "Industry: Petroleum wholesale and fuel distribution. Target audience: Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases. Tone: Direct, professional, no-nonsense — written from the perspective of experienced industry insiders, not salespeople. Emphasis on reliability, pricing transparency, and straightforward service. Purpose: Generate qualified B2B leads from fuel buyers who need a dependable wholesale distribution partner.", "social_profiles": {}, "target_audience": "Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases", "competitors_found": ["econogas.ca", "igasusa.com"], "has_existing_site": false, "existing_site_quality": "none", "unique_selling_points": ["Wholesale pricing for bulk fuel purchases", "Direct terminal access and distribution networks", "B2B focused fuel supply solutions", "Competitive rack pricing programs"], "target_audience_and_purpose": "Primary industry vertical: wholesale fuel distribution. Target audience segments: (1) forecourt operators and gas station owners purchasing bulk fuel for resale, (2) commercial fleet managers seeking reliable fuel supply contracts and rack pricing, (3) industrial facilities and large commercial buyers requiring consistent volume delivery. Site purpose: lead generation — drive qualified inbound inquiries from buyers who need a dependable wholesale fuel partner. All content decisions should be evaluated against these guardrails: does it speak to one of these three segments, does it reinforce reliability and transparency, and does it move a prospect toward a contact or inquiry action.", "tagline_and_product_terminology": "Replace the current tagline 'Wholesale Gas Supply Solutions' with one that reflects the full product scope, such as 'Wholesale Fuel, Natural Gas & Specialty Gas Distribution' or 'Complete Wholesale Fuel & Gas Supply.' Define three canonical product categories for use across all pages: (1) Wholesale Fuel Distribution — gasoline, diesel, and refined petroleum products; (2) Natural Gas Distribution — commercial and industrial natural gas supply; (3) Specialty Gases — any non-commodity gas products referenced on the services page. Enforce this terminology framework site-wide so homepage subheadlines, service descriptions, page titles, and meta descriptions all use the same category names without variation.", "industry, target_audience, tone, purpose": "industry: 'wholesale fuel distribution'; target_audience: 'fuel retailers, fleet operators, commercial and industrial buyers'; tone: 'direct and professional'; purpose: 'generate qualified inbound leads for bulk fuel supply contracts'"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 21:43:16.508694+00	2026-03-14 21:44:08.222516+00	content-gap-planner	f
ca15e084-ecde-4c64-8e57-c06faf72f65a	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "leopardess@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": ""}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": ""}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": ""}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": ""}], "site_brief": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration (technology services). Primary audience: Three personas — (1) CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments and working code, not slide decks; (2) Founders of B2B SaaS or professional services firms who are technically literate, lack an internal AI/ML team, and need a delivery partner who can own end-to-end build; (3) Operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses seeking practical automation of high-volume workflows without hiring a full data engineering team. All three personas are time-poor, results-driven, and respond to specificity, working demos, and clear ROI framing. Tone: Practical, direct, technically credible — the voice of engineers who build real systems, not consultants who produce reports. Conversion purpose: Generate qualified inbound leads and demo requests from UK businesses ready to commission AI agent or automation work, with a secondary goal of establishing technical authority through case studies, tools, and insights content.", "company_name": "Leopardess Consulting", "about_summary": "At Leopardess Consulting, we like building smart, hierarchical AI agent systems that help businesses adapt quickly and effectively. Using tools like Kubernetes for orchestration, Kafka for smooth messaging, and Postgres for reliable storage, we create solutions that automate complex workflows – think spinning up and launching full multipage websites on Cloudflare in no time. We're here to help you make the most of AI with practical, dependable approaches that suit your team.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Primary: CTOs, engineering leads, and technical founders at UK scale-ups and B2B SaaS companies who evaluate vendors on production credibility, stack depth, and delivery track record. Secondary: technically-literate business decision-makers capable of assessing system architecture and engineering quality. Non-technical SMB buyers are explicitly out of scope. All page copy — including the about hero — must address this audience exclusively. Remove any references to 'small businesses', 'busy teams', or 'digital presence without complexity' site-wide.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "brand_voice_guidelines": "The Leopardess name is a live brand asset and should be referenced naturally at least once per page through metaphor rather than explicit explanation. The leopardess archetype carries: speed (fast delivery, rapid iteration, no slow consulting cycles), precision (targeted solutions, no wasted motion, surgical automation), adaptability (hunts in complex terrain, works across stacks and sectors), and instinct (pattern recognition, knowing where to move before the client does). Apply these qualities to describe how the team works, how systems are built, and how problems are approached. Examples: 'We move fast because we've already mapped the terrain', 'precision-built agents, not broad-brush automation', 'we don't advise from the sidelines — we hunt the problem alongside you'. Avoid forced or literal animal references. The metaphor should feel like a natural extension of the practical-expert voice, not a mascot gimmick.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration / technology services. Target Audience: CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments; founders of B2B SaaS or professional services companies evaluating build-vs-buy for agent orchestration; operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses automating high-volume workflows. Tone: Direct, technically credible, evidence-led — the voice of practitioners who ship working systems, not consultants who produce decks. Purpose: Lead generation and service conversion, achieved by demonstrating technical depth, showing real production deployments, and giving time-poor technical buyers enough specificity to self-qualify and initiate contact."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 15:41:31.479075+00	2026-03-14 22:03:31.299881+00	content-gap-planner	f
81ee5776-d78f-4fdc-9478-17a74c865300	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	submission	{"domain": "vonc.com", "mission": {"mission": "AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game", "tagline": "TikTok is where you watch. Twitter is where you shout. Spark is where you play.", "positioning": "Not another social app. A daily game powered by what is happening in the world. You don't post. You don't scroll. You play.", "content_tone": {"is": ["interesting", "slightly adult", "competitive", "aspirational", "playful", "game-like", "energetic"], "is_not": ["dark", "gruesome", "violent", "xxx", "newspaper news", "corporate", "generic social media", "AI slop"], "ai_role": "Producer not performer. AI frames, scores, curates, synthesises. Never does humour, hot takes, sarcasm."}, "target_users": {"primary": "People with opinions on current trends but no platform that asks for them", "tertiary": "Curators and tastemakers — people who find things, not make things", "secondary": "Creators wanting skill showcase with built-in audience and niche discovery"}, "core_concepts": {"cold_start": "Solo mode fully functional for 1 person. AI sparring partner fills the room transparently.", "engage_first": "No signup walls, no explanations. A provocation card and a text input. Engage first, understand second, commit third.", "archetype_system": "Profile emerges from behaviour. Daily Gauntlet produces shareable archetype cards.", "ai_slop_awareness": "AI restricted to genuine strengths. Deliberately bad AI takes as challenge seeds.", "the_game_metaphor": "Everything is framed as a game. Challenges have timers, rules, scores, winners."}, "key_differentiators": ["AI as game master and producer, never the performer", "Opinion-first entry point — you need a take, not an idea", "Ephemeral challenges with permanent emergent reputation", "Rooms not feeds — enter a space with energy, don't scroll a stream", "Arena (competitive takes) + Stage (creative showcase) dual modes", "Archetypes earned from behaviour, not self-reported"], "measurable_objectives": [{"id": "obj_dau_50", "metric": "daily_active_users", "target": 50, "objective": "50 DAU within 4 weeks"}, {"id": "obj_gauntlet_rate", "metric": "gauntlet_completion_rate", "target": 0.15, "objective": "Gauntlet completion >15% of visitors"}, {"id": "obj_session_duration", "metric": "avg_session_duration_seconds", "target": 180, "objective": "Avg session >3 minutes"}, {"id": "obj_share_rate", "metric": "gauntlet_share_rate", "target": 0.05, "objective": ">5% Gauntlet completions shared"}]}, "roadmap": {"phases": {"v4_and_beyond": {"status": "speculative", "description": "Stage mode. Multi-format. Niche discovery. Monetisation."}, "v1_content_first": {"pages": [{"slug": "index", "purpose": "The product IS the landing page. Single provocation card filling screen. Text input beneath. Timer. No signup wall.", "priority": 1, "section_types": ["provocation-card", "lobby-grid", "brief-explanation", "gauntlet-cta"]}, {"slug": "provocations", "purpose": "Today's active provocations with AI takes. Each has shareable URL. SEO content. Card-based layout.", "priority": 2, "section_types": ["provocation-feed"]}, {"slug": "gauntlet", "purpose": "Daily Gauntlet — 5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. Client-side JS.", "priority": 3, "section_types": ["gauntlet-interface", "archetype-result-card"], "content_context": {"archetypes": [{"name": "The Surgeon", "tagline": "Precise, analytical, cuts to the core", "strengths": "Analytical speed, structural clarity, finding hidden flaws", "description": "Strips arguments to essential structure. Fast on logical frameworks."}, {"name": "The Wildcard", "tagline": "Unpredictable, highest remix rate", "strengths": "Creative leaps, remix ability, cross-domain thinking", "description": "Takes ideas in unexpected directions. Crosses domains freely."}, {"name": "The Oracle", "tagline": "Quiet but accurate, rare but impactful", "strengths": "Prediction accuracy, timing, selective engagement", "description": "Does not respond often but when they do it lands. Best prediction accuracy."}, {"name": "The Catalyst", "tagline": "Responses generate longest chains", "strengths": "Provocation, opening angles, generating momentum", "description": "Individual responses might not be best, but they spark others."}, {"name": "The Judge", "tagline": "Spectates, but reactions predict outcomes", "strengths": "Pattern recognition, taste, predictive judgement", "description": "Lives in the Gallery. Reaction pattern most predictive of final outcomes."}, {"name": "The Maker", "tagline": "Stage-dominant, consistent showcaser", "strengths": "Creative output, consistency, skill demonstration", "description": "Shows up with creations not opinions. Demonstrates skill."}, {"name": "The Scout", "tagline": "Identifies breakout creators early", "strengths": "Early identification, taste, discovery", "description": "The curator. Finds things others miss."}, {"name": "The Mentor", "tagline": "Breakdowns among most saved content", "strengths": "Teaching, explanation, knowledge sharing", "description": "Explanations are teaching material. Turns admiration into learning."}], "gauntlet_mechanics": "5 provocations mixing opinion and creation prompts. Scored on response speed, originality, consistency, topic preferences. Produces primary archetype with secondary tendencies. Shareable visual card."}}, {"slug": "about", "purpose": "What Spark is. Quick, energetic explanation. Game metaphor. Arena vs Stage. AI game master concept.", "priority": 4, "section_types": ["hero", "platform-comparison", "game-master-explanation", "gauntlet-cta"], "content_context": {"key_comparisons": {"vs_reddit": "Reddit: permanent, karma-hierarchical, dominated by early commenters. Spark: ephemeral, anonymised during play, scored on quality not timing.", "vs_tiktok": "TikTok: passive consumption, massive creator/consumer divide. Spark: opinion entry point, Gauntlet proves anyone can participate in 5 minutes.", "vs_twitter": "Twitter: shouting into a void. Spark: put in a room where engagement is guaranteed."}, "game_master_explanation": "AI does not try to be funny or clever. AI runs the game: finds what is interesting (scraping), frames it sharply (provocation), keeps score (reputation, archetypes), synthesises results (recaps). Humans bring wit and creativity. AI builds the arena."}}, {"slug": "archetypes", "purpose": "Archetype system explained. Each gets section with name, tagline, description, strengths. Shareable individual cards.", "priority": 5, "section_types": ["hero", "archetype-grid", "archetype-combinations"], "content_context": {"combination_examples": ["Surgeon-Oracle: Rarely speaks, but precisely targeted insight that predicts outcomes", "Wildcard-Catalyst: Unexpected ideas everyone wants to riff on", "Maker-Mentor: Creates consistently and teaches others to improve", "Scout-Judge: Does not create or opine, but most trusted taste on the platform"]}}], "status": "active", "hosting": "s3_static", "features": ["daily_provocation_generation_from_scraping", "ai_take_per_provocation", "shareable_provocation_cards", "daily_gauntlet_client_side", "archetype_generation_and_share_cards", "daily_static_regeneration"], "description": "Static S3 site. Provocations as SEO content. Daily Gauntlet as viral archetype quiz.", "design_direction": "Game energy, not corporate. Dark theme with vibrant accents. Cards, timers, energy indicators. Arena lobby feel. Mobile-first.", "success_criteria": {"daily_visitors": 50, "avg_session_seconds": 180, "gauntlet_completion_rate": 0.15}}, "v3_rooms_and_community": {"status": "speculative", "description": "Live challenge rooms. Arena mode. Chains. Duels. Reputation."}, "v2_sparring_and_interaction": {"status": "directional", "description": "AI sparring on provocations. User accounts. Live reactions."}}, "current_phase": "v1_content_first"}, "objective": "Build a content-first launch site for Spark, an AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game. V1 is static S3 with daily provocation generation and a viral archetype quiz. The landing page IS the product.", "mission_brief": {"text": "Spark is an AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game.\\n\\nPositioning: Not another social app. A daily game powered by what is happening in the world. You don't post. You don't scroll. You play.\\n\\nTagline: TikTok is where you watch. Twitter is where you shout. Spark is where you play.\\n\\nKey differentiators:\\n- AI as game master and producer, never the performer — when something is funny or impressive, a human did it\\n- Opinion-first entry point — you need a take, not an idea\\n- Ephemeral challenges with permanent emergent reputation — disposable content, lasting identity\\n- Rooms not feeds — enter a space with energy, don't scroll a stream\\n- Arena (competitive takes) + Stage (creative showcase) dual modes\\n- Archetypes earned from behaviour, not self-reported — your profile emerges from how you engage\\n\\nTarget users:\\n- Primary: People with opinions on current trends but no platform that asks for them\\n- Secondary: Creators wanting skill showcase with built-in audience and niche discovery\\n- Tertiary: Curators and tastemakers — people who find things, not make things\\n\\nContent tone: interesting, slightly adult, competitive, aspirational, playful, game-like, energetic\\nNot: dark, gruesome, violent, corporate, generic social media, AI slop\\nAI role: Producer not performer. AI frames, scores, curates, synthesises. Never does humour, hot takes, sarcasm."}, "roadmap_brief": {"text": "Current phase: v1_content_first\\nStatic S3 site. Provocations as SEO content. Daily Gauntlet as viral archetype quiz.\\nDesign: Game energy, not corporate. Dark theme with vibrant accents. Cards, timers, energy indicators. Arena lobby feel. Mobile-first.\\n\\nPages for this phase:\\n- index: The product IS the landing page. Single provocation card filling screen. Text input beneath. Timer. No signup wall.\\n  Sections: provocation-card, lobby-grid, brief-explanation, gauntlet-cta\\n- provocations: Today's active provocations with AI takes. Each has shareable URL. SEO content. Card-based layout.\\n  Sections: provocation-feed\\n- gauntlet: Daily Gauntlet — 5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. Client-side JS. Produces shareable archetype card.\\n  Sections: gauntlet-interface, archetype-result-card\\n- about: What Spark is. Quick, energetic explanation. Game metaphor. Arena vs Stage. AI game master concept. How archetypes work.\\n  Sections: hero, platform-comparison, game-master-explanation, gauntlet-cta\\n- archetypes: Archetype system explained. Each gets section with name, tagline, description, strengths. Shareable individual cards.\\n  Sections: hero, archetype-grid, archetype-combinations\\n\\nFuture phases (not for building now):\\n- v2: AI sparring on provocations, user accounts, live reactions\\n- v3: Live challenge rooms, arena mode, chains, duels, reputation\\n- v4: Stage mode, monetisation, vertical integration"}}	domain-submitter	domain-submitter	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 09:49:00.231106+00	\N	domain-submitter	f
75808a40-0b0b-4fd3-978f-1197ddd1fc92	5fe15466-4e2e-4ff2-981e-98c1b7074002	voice	{"brand_language_rules": "Reserve the phrase 'without the runaround' exclusively for the homepage hero. Do not repeat it on services, about, contact, or any other page. Each page must lead with its own differentiating angle: services page should lead with reliability metrics or delivery coverage scope; about page should lead with industry tenure, team credentials, or years in operation; contact page should emphasize response speed or direct access to a real person. Repetition of the same hero phrase across multiple pages signals templated content and undermines the no-nonsense, intentional brand voice."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 14:57:55.996987+00	2026-03-14 23:53:20.571307+00	content-gap-planner	f
aedb8a72-313c-4617-86f5-25e51bf31169	5fe15466-4e2e-4ff2-981e-98c1b7074002	identity	{"email": "gas@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "contact": {"email": null, "phone": null, "address": null, "location": null}, "tagline": null, "industry": "Energy & Fuel Distribution", "services": [{"name": "Wholesale Fuel Distribution", "description": "Bulk supply of gasoline and diesel to retailers and commercial clients"}, {"name": "Fleet Fuel Services", "description": "Fuel supply solutions for commercial fleet operations"}, {"name": "Natural Gas Distribution", "description": "Wholesale natural gas supply to industrial and commercial customers"}, {"name": "Rack Pricing Programs", "description": "Wholesale rack fuel pricing for resellers and distributors"}], "key_people": [], "company_name": "Gas Wholesalers", "sub_industry": "Wholesale Gas & Petroleum Products", "about_summary": "Gas Wholesalers appears to be a wholesale distribution company focused on gas and petroleum products. Based on the domain name and industry research, this likely involves the wholesale supply of gasoline, diesel, natural gas, or related energy products to retailers, fleet operators, or industrial clients. The company would operate in the B2B fuel distribution market.", "site_strategy": "Industry: Petroleum wholesale and fuel distribution. Target audience: Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases. Tone: Direct, professional, no-nonsense — written from the perspective of experienced industry insiders, not salespeople. Emphasis on reliability, pricing transparency, and straightforward service. Purpose: Generate qualified B2B leads from fuel buyers who need a dependable wholesale distribution partner.", "social_profiles": {}, "target_audience": "Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and businesses requiring bulk fuel purchases", "competitors_found": ["econogas.ca", "igasusa.com"], "has_existing_site": false, "existing_site_quality": "none", "unique_selling_points": ["Wholesale pricing for bulk fuel purchases", "Direct terminal access and distribution networks", "B2B focused fuel supply solutions", "Competitive rack pricing programs"], "target_audience_and_purpose": "Primary industry vertical: wholesale fuel distribution. Target audience segments: (1) forecourt operators and gas station owners purchasing bulk fuel for resale, (2) commercial fleet managers seeking reliable fuel supply contracts and rack pricing, (3) industrial facilities and large commercial buyers requiring consistent volume delivery. Site purpose: lead generation — drive qualified inbound inquiries from buyers who need a dependable wholesale fuel partner. All content decisions should be evaluated against these guardrails: does it speak to one of these three segments, does it reinforce reliability and transparency, and does it move a prospect toward a contact or inquiry action.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: Wholesale fuel distribution and natural gas supply. Target Audience: Gas station owners, fuel retailers, commercial fleet operators, industrial facilities, convenience store chains, and bulk fuel buyers. Tone: Experienced industry insiders — direct, no-nonsense, transparent, and reliability-focused; avoid salesy or overly promotional language. Primary Conversion Purpose: Drive qualified bulk fuel buyers and fleet operators to request pricing or initiate a supply relationship via contact or rack pricing inquiry.", "tagline_and_product_terminology": "Replace the current tagline 'Wholesale Gas Supply Solutions' with one that reflects the full product scope, such as 'Wholesale Fuel, Natural Gas & Specialty Gas Distribution' or 'Complete Wholesale Fuel & Gas Supply.' Define three canonical product categories for use across all pages: (1) Wholesale Fuel Distribution — gasoline, diesel, and refined petroleum products; (2) Natural Gas Distribution — commercial and industrial natural gas supply; (3) Specialty Gases — any non-commodity gas products referenced on the services page. Enforce this terminology framework site-wide so homepage subheadlines, service descriptions, page titles, and meta descriptions all use the same category names without variation.", "industry, target_audience, tone, purpose": "industry: 'wholesale fuel distribution'; target_audience: 'fuel retailers, fleet operators, commercial and industrial buyers'; tone: 'direct and professional'; purpose: 'generate qualified inbound leads for bulk fuel supply contracts'"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 21:44:08.226522+00	2026-03-15 00:10:53.844657+00	content-gap-planner	f
64f89bff-114e-4be5-9e53-53d7330c4c3d	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "leopardess@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": ""}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": ""}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": ""}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": ""}], "site_brief": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration (technology services). Primary audience: Three personas — (1) CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments and working code, not slide decks; (2) Founders of B2B SaaS or professional services firms who are technically literate, lack an internal AI/ML team, and need a delivery partner who can own end-to-end build; (3) Operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses seeking practical automation of high-volume workflows without hiring a full data engineering team. All three personas are time-poor, results-driven, and respond to specificity, working demos, and clear ROI framing. Tone: Practical, direct, technically credible — the voice of engineers who build real systems, not consultants who produce reports. Conversion purpose: Generate qualified inbound leads and demo requests from UK businesses ready to commission AI agent or automation work, with a secondary goal of establishing technical authority through case studies, tools, and insights content.", "company_name": "Leopardess Consulting", "about_summary": "At Leopardess Consulting, we like building smart, hierarchical AI agent systems that help businesses adapt quickly and effectively. Using tools like Kubernetes for orchestration, Kafka for smooth messaging, and Postgres for reliable storage, we create solutions that automate complex workflows – think spinning up and launching full multipage websites on Cloudflare in no time. We're here to help you make the most of AI with practical, dependable approaches that suit your team.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Primary: CTOs, engineering leads, and technical founders at UK scale-ups and B2B SaaS companies who evaluate vendors on production credibility, stack depth, and delivery track record. Secondary: technically-literate business decision-makers capable of assessing system architecture and engineering quality. Non-technical SMB buyers are explicitly out of scope.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "brand_voice_guidelines": "The Leopardess name is a live brand asset and should be referenced naturally at least once per page through metaphor rather than explicit explanation. The leopardess archetype carries: speed (fast delivery, rapid iteration, no slow consulting cycles), precision (targeted solutions, no wasted motion, surgical automation), adaptability (hunts in complex terrain, works across stacks and sectors), and instinct (pattern recognition, knowing where to move before the client does). Apply these qualities to describe how the team works, how systems are built, and how problems are approached. Examples: 'We move fast because we've already mapped the terrain', 'precision-built agents, not broad-brush automation', 'we don't advise from the sidelines — we hunt the problem alongside you'. Avoid forced or literal animal references. The metaphor should feel like a natural extension of the practical-expert voice, not a mascot gimmick.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI consulting and agent orchestration / technology services. Target Audience: CTOs and engineering leads at UK scale-ups (50–500 employees) who need proof of production deployments; founders of B2B SaaS or professional services companies evaluating build-vs-buy for agent orchestration; operations and transformation leads at mid-market UK businesses automating high-volume workflows. Tone: Direct, technically credible, evidence-led — the voice of practitioners who ship working systems, not consultants who produce decks. Purpose: Lead generation and service conversion, achieved by demonstrating technical depth, showing real production deployments, and giving time-poor technical buyers enough specificity to self-qualify and initiate contact."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 22:03:31.305844+00	2026-03-15 01:39:12.72388+00	content-gap-planner	f
77a8ae45-a293-4d11-a25c-7938899f950b	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	audience	{"target_audience": "Primary: CTOs, engineering leads, and technical founders at UK scale-ups and B2B SaaS companies who evaluate vendors on production credibility, stack depth, and delivery track record. Secondary: technically-literate business decision-makers capable of assessing system architecture and engineering quality. Non-technical SMB buyers are explicitly out of scope. All copy should assume the reader can interpret references to Kubernetes, Kafka, Postgres, agent orchestration, and CI/CD pipelines without explanation. Remove or rewrite any language that frames the value proposition around saving time, working smarter, or growing your business as these patterns signal SME-targeting and undermine credibility with technical evaluators."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 22:05:43.445688+00	2026-03-15 02:14:44.78404+00	content-gap-planner	f
cb1f7f00-1566-4e54-82f3-6ca00bb8c9ab	2a8ebf9c-20a2-4c39-b191-840b012371da	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "agents@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": "Get production-ready websites up and running in minutes with our AI-powered multi-agent systems. We handle secure, scalable hosting on Cloudflare, including automated builds, testing, and launches – removing the usual hurdles so you can focus on what matters."}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": "We design custom hierarchical agent setups to address your business challenges. Supporting a range of LLMs and models, these systems delegate tasks sensibly, collaborate in real time, and scale smoothly for effective automation."}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": "Clear guidance to integrate AI and modern technology into your everyday operations. We work with you to build straightforward roadmaps for AI adoption, streamlining workflows, and staying agile in a fast-changing world."}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": "Practical advice on modern web architectures, smart deployment, and useful AI integrations. We help your team build solid, forward-thinking web applications that focus on speed, security, and real innovation."}], "company_name": "AI Agent Orchestration", "about_summary": "AI Agent Orchestration builds production-grade multi-agent systems on proven infrastructure — Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres. We design hierarchical agent architectures that automate complex workflows, from automated website deployment to real-time agent collaboration. No demos. No slide decks. Working systems, deployed and running.", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "CTOs, engineering leads, and technology decision-makers at mid-to-large enterprises and scaling startups who are evaluating or actively deploying AI agent systems in production environments. Secondary audience includes startup founders and forward-thinking business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable outcomes.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "target_audience_tone_purpose": "Target Audience: CTOs, engineering leads, VP Engineering, and technically sophisticated startup founders evaluating production AI infrastructure. Secondary: forward-thinking business owners who understand technology investment. Tone: Direct, confident, and technically credible — written by builders for builders. No fluff, no vague consulting language. Purpose: Lead generation and consultation bookings for AI agent orchestration engagements, supported by demonstration of deep technical competence through case studies, tooling, and blog content.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI infrastructure and enterprise automation consulting. Target audience: Platform engineers, AI architects, CTOs, and technology leaders at mid-to-large enterprises evaluating or scaling multi-agent AI systems. Tone: Technical, direct, and credibility-first — written by builders for buyers who can tell the difference between real deployments and slide-deck consulting. Purpose: Lead generation for high-value consulting engagements focused on production-grade AI agent orchestration using Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres stacks."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 15:26:59.551851+00	2026-03-15 08:48:22.303124+00	content-gap-planner	f
3b1f0dfc-8dec-4176-9260-eb6dae570b90	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	identity	{"tone": "conversational, direct, anti-corporate", "email": "finetuning@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "AI for the Rest of Us", "industry": "AI consulting / technology services", "multiple": "industry: AI consulting and technology services | target_audience: UK SMEs including managing directors, operations managers, and technical founders seeking practical AI implementation | tone: plain-speaking, anti-hype, practitioner-led — direct and honest without jargon or inflated claims | purpose: lead generation for custom AI projects, positioning FineTuning as the credible no-nonsense alternative to big consultancies for businesses that want results not presentations", "company_name": "FineTuning", "tone_of_voice": "Plain-spoken and direct. We write like experienced practitioners talking to a busy business owner, not like a tech vendor pitching to a CTO. No buzzwords, no hype, no jargon without explanation. Confident but not arrogant. We acknowledge AI limitations honestly. Short sentences preferred. Active voice. UK English spelling. Avoid: 'leverage', 'cutting-edge', 'transformative', 'unlock', 'harness', 'game-changing', 'AI-powered' as a standalone claim. When in doubt, ask: would a sceptical SME owner roll their eyes at this? If yes, rewrite it.", "target_audience": "UK SME owners and senior managers with 5–50 employees, typically non-technical, who are curious about AI but sceptical of hype. They want honest, practical advice on where AI can genuinely save time or money in their business — not a technology lecture. Primary conversion goal is to book a discovery call. Industry verticals are broad but may skew toward professional services, retail, and light manufacturing where operational efficiency gains are most tangible.", "content_strategy": "Target audience: UK SME owners and managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical but commercially minded. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — no jargon, no hype, honest about what AI can and cannot do. Purpose: lead generation via consultation bookings, supported by trust-building content. Industry: AI consulting and advisory services. All content should speak directly to time-poor business owners who are sceptical of tech vendors and want straight answers.", "editorial_metadata": "target_audience: UK SME owners and senior managers (5–50 employees), non-technical, sceptical of hype, seeking practical AI guidance; tone: plain-speaking, pragmatic, no jargon, experienced-practitioner voice; purpose: lead generation via discovery call bookings; industry: AI consulting and technology services for UK SMEs, with emphasis on professional services, retail, and light manufacturing"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-14 13:41:37.610581+00	2026-03-14 22:37:40.354522+00	content-gap-planner	f
