2825bfb9-1cc8-4d81-9922-f878d101585a	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	identity	{"tone": "conversational, direct, anti-corporate", "email": "finetuning@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "AI for the Rest of Us", "industry": "AI consulting / technology services", "multiple": "industry: AI consulting and technology services | target_audience: UK SMEs including managing directors, operations managers, and technical founders seeking practical AI implementation | tone: plain-speaking, anti-hype, practitioner-led — direct and honest without jargon or inflated claims | purpose: lead generation for custom AI projects, positioning FineTuning as the credible no-nonsense alternative to big consultancies for businesses that want results not presentations", "company_name": "FineTuning", "content_brief": "Primary audience: UK SME owners and senior managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical, sceptical of AI hype, looking for honest and practical guidance on where AI can genuinely save time or money. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — the voice of an experienced practitioner who has no interest in overselling. No jargon, no buzzwords, no breathless enthusiasm. Site purpose: generate discovery call bookings by building trust with an audience that has been burned by vague AI promises before. Every page should either educate, reassure, or move the reader toward booking a call. Industry verticals: broad UK SME, with emphasis on professional services, retail, and light manufacturing where operational efficiency gains are most tangible.", "site_metadata": "ICP: UK SME owners and senior managers, 5–50 employees, service-based industries, non-technical, time-poor, sceptical of vendor hype. Tone: plain-spoken, direct, no-nonsense, practitioner credibility — no buzzwords, no jargon, real numbers where possible. Primary conversion goal: book a free consultation or initial call via the contact page. Secondary goal: build trust through honest, practical content so visitors self-qualify before reaching out.", "tone_of_voice": "Plain-spoken and direct. We write like experienced practitioners talking to a busy business owner, not like a tech vendor pitching to a CTO. No buzzwords, no hype, no jargon without explanation. Confident but not arrogant. We acknowledge AI limitations honestly. Short sentences preferred. Active voice. UK English spelling. Avoid: 'leverage', 'cutting-edge', 'transformative', 'unlock', 'harness', 'game-changing', 'AI-powered' as a standalone claim. When in doubt, ask: would a sceptical SME owner roll their eyes at this? If yes, rewrite it.", "target_audience": "UK SME owners and senior managers at businesses with 5–50 employees, typically in service-based industries. Non-technical decision-makers who are curious about AI but sceptical of vendor hype. They want honest, practical guidance on where AI can save them time or money — not a technology lecture. They respond to plain English, real numbers, and proof that something works before they commit.", "content_strategy": "Target audience: UK SME owners and managers, typically 5–50 employees, non-technical but commercially minded. Tone: plain-spoken, pragmatic, reassuring — no jargon, no hype, honest about what AI can and cannot do. Purpose: lead generation via consultation bookings, supported by trust-building content. Industry: AI consulting and advisory services. All content should speak directly to time-poor business owners who are sceptical of tech vendors and want straight answers.", "editorial_metadata": "target_audience: UK SME owners and senior managers (5–50 employees), non-technical, sceptical of hype, seeking practical AI guidance; tone: plain-speaking, pragmatic, no jargon, experienced-practitioner voice; purpose: lead generation via discovery call bookings; industry: AI consulting and technology services for UK SMEs, with emphasis on professional services, retail, and light manufacturing"}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-pla