09d32f12-7d1e-4ec5-8db2-c2c5e339c8c9	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	briefing	{"gaps": ["contact_email", "contact_phone", "headquarters", "leadership_team", "case_studies"], "tone": "bold", "tagline": "TikTok is where you watch. Twitter is where you shout. Spark is where you play.", "about_us": "Spark is an AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game. Not another social app. A daily game powered by what is happening in the world. You don't post. You don't scroll. You play.\\n\\nSpark positions itself at the intersection of game mechanics, opinion expression, and ephemeral challenge rooms. AI serves as game master and producer — it frames provocations, keeps score, curates content, and synthesises results. When something is funny or impressive, a human did it.\\n\\nThe platform combines Arena mode (competitive takes) and Stage mode (creative showcase) with a behavioural archetype system. Your profile emerges from how you engage, not from what you claim to be. Ephemeral challenges produce permanent emergent reputation.\\n\\nSpark is built for people with opinions on current trends but no platform that asks for them, creators wanting skill showcase with built-in audience, and curators who find things rather than make them.", "has_blog": false, "industry": "Social Platform / Interactive Media", "services": [{"name": "Daily Provocations", "description": "AI-generated provocations pulled from real-world events. Each provocation is a shareable card with a text input, timer, and AI take. The world provides the content — you provide the take."}, {"name": "Daily Gauntlet", "description": "5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. A client-side interactive quiz that mixes opinion and creation prompts, scored on response speed, originality, consistency, and topic preferences. Produces a shareable archetype card."}, {"name": "Archetype System", "description": "8 behavioural archetypes earned through engagement: The Surgeon, The Wildcard, The Oracle, The Catalyst, The Judge, The Maker, The Scout, The Mentor. Your profile emerges from how you play, not from self-reported traits."}, {"name": "Arena Mode", "description": "Competitive opinion space where takes are scored, compared, and synthesised. Enter a room with energy — don't scroll a stream. Engagement is guaranteed."}, {"name": "Stage Mode", "description": "Creative showcase space for skill demonstration. Built for makers who show up with creations, not opinions. Niche discovery through consistent output."}], "site_type": "landing-page", "has_careers": false, "case_studies": null, "company_name": "VONC", "headquarters": null, "contact_email": "[INFERRED] hello@vonc.com", "contact_phone": null, "leadership_team": null, "briefing_confidence": 0.92, "recommended_builder": "pageflow-builder"}	build-briefing-agent	build-briefing-agent	\N	\N	f	2026-04-02 09:55:53.039779+00	2026-04-02 11:43:47.131521+00	build-briefing-agent	f
58cf1337-79d6-415b-b365-8c172b2d6f1b	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	editorial	{"tone_guide": "Voice: Experienced practitioners who cut through AI hype. Write as a trusted advisor talking to a busy SME owner — not a vendor, not a lecturer. Use plain English throughout. Avoid buzzwords (transformation, leverage, synergy, cutting-edge, revolutionary). Prefer concrete over abstract: real numbers, specific outcomes, named tasks over vague capability claims. Scepticism is a feature: acknowledge where AI falls short, where it is overhyped, or where it is not the right tool. Never oversell. Sentences should be short to medium length. Paragraphs should be short. Active voice preferred. Contractions are fine and encouraged. Humour is acceptable but dry — never forced. The reader is smart but not technical. Never make them feel stupid for not knowing something. UK English spelling and conventions throughout (e.g. optimise not optimize, licence not license). When in doubt, ask: would a no-nonsense operations manager at a 20-person UK firm find this useful and credible? If not, rewrite it."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-17 18:04:15.483958+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
5be3d2c3-6d14-4310-957f-3bb6be23bfb3	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	voice	{"tone_guardrails": "Maintain direct, anti-hype voice across all pages including commercial ones (pricing, services). Avoid corporate-speak drift. Permitted: plain English, honest caveats, real numbers, dry wit. Not permitted: synergy-style language, vague superlatives, vendor-speak, padding. Pricing and services pages should read like advice from a trusted practitioner, not a sales brochure. Review any new page draft against existing posts such as 'AI Tools We Wouldn't Recommend' and 'AI Won't Save Your Business' as tone benchmarks."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-17 18:06:33.661198+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
79dd370b-9627-42da-9935-f7b79be37433	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	voice_and_tone	{"tone_guidelines": "Plain-spoken, direct, and anti-hype throughout. Write as an experienced practitioner talking to a busy SME owner — not a technology vendor. Avoid AI industry jargon (do not use: leverage, cutting-edge, transformative, unlock, empower, harness, robust, scalable, ecosystem, or similar). Use short sentences. Favour concrete numbers and real outcomes over abstract claims. Acknowledge limitations honestly — if AI won't help in a given situation, say so. The brand voice markers 'No sales pitch, no jargon' and 'We tell you when AI won't help' should feel true on every page. Blog posts and case studies are highest-risk for tone drift — review these against this standard before publishing. If a sentence would not sound out of place in a vendor press release, rewrite it."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-17 18:02:27.484399+00	2026-03-17 18:34:17.104624+00	content-gap-planner	f
bc6b991f-c90b-4a3e-a700-fbbb7b185322	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	voice_and_tone	{"tone_definition": "Plain-spoken, sceptical of hype, practitioner-led. Write as an experienced consultant who has seen AI projects fail and succeed, and has no interest in overselling. Use short sentences. Prefer concrete examples and real numbers over abstract claims. Avoid: buzzwords (leverage, unlock, harness, empower, transform, cutting-edge, game-changer, seamless, robust, scalable, innovative), passive constructions that obscure accountability, feature-listing without benefit context, and any phrasing that sounds like a vendor brochure. Red-flag review trigger: if a sentence could appear unchanged on a generic SaaS marketing page, rewrite it. Tone checks should be applied to all new service descriptions, use case entries, and blog posts before publication.", "tone_guidelines": "Plain-spoken, direct, and anti-hype throughout. Write as an experienced practitioner talking to a busy SME owner — not a technology vendor. Avoid AI industry jargon (do not use: leverage, cutting-edge, transformative, unlock, empower, harness, robust, scalable, ecosystem, or similar). Use short sentences. Favour concrete numbers and real outcomes over abstract claims. Acknowledge limitations honestly — if AI won't help in a given situation, say so. The brand voice markers 'No sales pitch, no jargon' and 'We tell you when AI won't help' should feel true on every page. Blog posts and case studies are highest-risk for tone drift — review these against this standard before publishing. If a sentence would not sound out of place in a vendor press release, rewrite it."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-03-17 18:34:17.113598+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
e0254c99-96c9-4521-be51-f75a741530e6	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	site_plan	{"response": {"pages": [{"name": "index", "title": "FineTuning | AI Systems That Actually Do The Work", "sections": ["hero", "differentiators-section", "services-grid", "social_proof", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Home", "nav_order": 1}, {"name": "services", "title": "Services | FineTuning", "sections": ["services-hero", "services-grid", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Services", "nav_order": 2}, {"name": "approach", "title": "Our Approach | FineTuning", "sections": ["hero", "features", "differentiators-section", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Approach", "nav_order": 3}, {"name": "use-cases", "title": "Use Cases | FineTuning", "sections": ["use-cases-hero", "use-cases-list", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Use Cases", "nav_order": 4}, {"name": "about", "title": "About Us | FineTuning", "sections": ["about-hero", "about-content", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "About", "nav_order": 5}, {"name": "contact", "title": "Contact Us | FineTuning", "sections": ["contact-hero", "contact-form", "contact-info"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Contact", "nav_order": 6}], "needs_logo": true, "needs_images": true, "image_prompts": {"logo": "A modern, technical logo for an AI systems company called FineTuning. Use clean, precise geometric shapes suggesting neural networks or system architecture with a color palette of deep navy blue, electric blue, and white. The design should convey technical competence, precision, and practical engineering rather than flashy tech aesthetics.", "hero_home": "A sophisticated, technical background with abstract representations of interconnected systems and data flows. Use deep navy blue and electric blue tones with subtle gradients and geometric network patterns that suggest AI agents working together. The mood should be professional, intelligent, and focused on real-world problem-solving rather than futuristic fantasy. Include subtle grid patterns or circuit-like elements that convey systematic engineering."}, "style_collection": "professional-dark"}, "response_status": "complete", "response_received_at": "2026-03-19T17:09:40Z"}	pageflow-builder	site-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-19 17:10:09.091544+00	2026-03-20 00:09:48.56144+00	site-planner	f
4cf7df45-452c-4b99-8b00-e34417a9fd2d	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	briefing	{"tagline": "From idea to AI system", "about_us": "  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our aim is to make AI genuinely useful.   ## AI systems that actually do the work  Most companies experimenting with AI end up with prototypes, demos, or chatbots.  Very few end up with systems that **save time, automate work, or generate measurable value**.  Finetune helps organisations design and deploy practical AI systems — automation pipelines, specialised models, and intelligent agents that solve real operational problems.  Not AI theatre.  ---  Real systems.  # Rapid experimentation  AI technology is moving quickly.  The companies that benefit most are those that can **experiment cheaply and deploy quickly**.  We aim to make it easy to test ideas, build prototypes, and evolve them into real systems when they prove useful.   ---  # What we build  We work with companies to build AI infrastructure that fits into real workflows.  ### Automation systems  AI that screens requests, processes documents, extracts information, and routes work automatically.  ### Intelligent agent pipelines  Systems where multiple AI agents collaborate to solve problems, analyse information, or complete complex tasks.  ### Custom AI models  Fine-tuned models trained on domain-specific data using techniques such as LoRA and other efficient training methods.  ### RAG systems for company knowledge  AI that can search and reason over internal data such as documents, emails, financial information, and knowledge bases.  ### Private AI deployments  Secure systems where models can run locally or within controlled environments to protect sensitive data.  ### Data collection infrastructure  Large-scale web data pipelines capable of gathering structured information from thousands of sources.  ---  # Why most AI projects fail  Many AI initiatives stall for predictable reasons.  **They start with tools instead of problems.**  **They stay in prototype mode.**  **They rely on third-party systems that can’t integrate with existing workflows.**  **Or they assume a single AI model will magically solve everything.**  In practice, useful AI systems usually require:  * data pipelines * automation layers * model adaptation * monitoring and iteration  AI works best as **part of a system**, not as a standalone tool.  ---  # The Finetune approach  We focus on **practical deployment**.  That means starting with a real operational problem and designing a system around it.  A typical project might involve:  1. Collecting and structuring the relevant data 2. Building automation pipelines 3. Training or adapting models 4. Integrating the system into existing workflows 5. Iterating until the system reliably saves time or improves decisions  The goal is not simply to use AI.  The goal is to make something **genuinely useful**.  ---  # What we can help with  Examples of problems we help solve:  * Screening and routing incoming requests * Automating quoting or proposal workflows * Extracting structured information from documents * Building internal knowledge assistants * Collecting market or financial data at scale * Deploying private AI models for sensitive workflows * Setting up agent pipelines that can perform complex multi-step tasks  Some systems are simple and highly targeted.  Others involve networks of cooperating agents and large-scale data pipelines.  ---  # A note on scale  We are particularly interested in **agent systems and large-scale automation**.  This includes experimentation with environments where thousands of AI agents can communicate and collaborate to solve problems.  These systems are still emerging, but they point toward a future where much of the routine work inside organisations can be handled by coordinated software agents.  Our goal is to help companies begin exploring that future in a practical way.  ---    ---  # Who we work with  We tend to work best with organisations that:  * have complex workflows or data * are open to experimentation * want to build internal capability with AI rather than just outsource it  This includes startups, established companies, and technical teams exploring new ways to operate.  ---  # About Finetune  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our focus is simple:  **make AI genuinely useful inside real organisations.**  ---  # Call to action  ## Curious what AI could automate in your business?  We’re always happy to have a technical conversation about possible approaches.  Contact us to discuss your workflows, data, or ideas.", "services": [{"name": "AI Automation Systems  ", "description": "Design and deployment of AI-driven automation pipelines that remove manual work from business processes. Examples include request screening, automated quoting, document analysis, and workflow orchestration."}, {"name": "Intelligent Agent Systems", "description": "Design and deployment of networks of AI agents capable of solving complex tasks collaboratively. These systems can analyse information, communicate with each other, and perform large-scale problem solving. Talk to us about systems capable of running tens of thousands of AI agents communicating with each other to solve complex tasks."}, {"name": "Custom AI Model Training", "description": "Training specialised models using techniques such as LoRA, DoRA, and other parameter-efficient methods to adapt modern AI models to your company's specific needs."}, {"name": "RAG Systems for Company Data", "description": "Deployment of Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems that allow AI to search and reason over your internal data including:  Emails  Documents  Financial records  Marketing material  Knowledge bases"}, {"name": "Bulk Data Collection", "description": "Large-scale web data extraction across thousands of websites, including structured business and financial data collection."}, {"name": "Financial and Company Data Pipelines", "description": "Automated systems for collecting and analysing financial data from public sources including company registries and regulatory filings."}, {"name": "Private AI Deployments", "description": "Secure deployment of AI systems that run privately — including models that can run locally or in-browser to protect company data and reduce usage costs."}, {"name": "Agent Pipeline Infrastructure", "description": "Installation and configuration of agent frameworks and orchestration systems so companies can run their own AI agents in production."}, {"name": "Rapid Website Generation", "description": "Creation of complex, high-quality static websites within minutes for:  company identity  marketing pages  landing pages  documentation  presentations"}, {"name": "AI Strategy & Implementation", "description": "Hands-on support helping companies move from curiosity about AI to systems that actually work inside their business."}, {"name": "High-Volume Data Acquisition", "description": "Design systems capable of collecting structured information from thousands of websites automatically."}], "company_name": "FineTuning"}	pageflow-builder	briefing-agent	\N	\N	f	2026-03-17 20:20:27.529491+00	2026-03-17 21:02:24.1858+00	briefing-agent	f
979bc3c0-7675-4996-bc1b-32394e733f8f	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	site_plan	{"response": {"pages": [{"name": "index", "title": "Finetune | AI Systems That Actually Work", "sections": ["hero", "differentiators-section", "services-grid", "social_proof", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Home", "nav_order": 1}, {"name": "services", "title": "Services | Finetune", "sections": ["services-hero", "services-grid", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Services", "nav_order": 2}, {"name": "approach", "title": "Our Approach | Finetune", "sections": ["hero", "features", "differentiators-section", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Approach", "nav_order": 3}, {"name": "use-cases", "title": "Use Cases | Finetune", "sections": ["use-cases-hero", "use-cases-list", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Use Cases", "nav_order": 4}, {"name": "about", "title": "About Us | Finetune", "sections": ["about-hero", "about-content", "call_to_action"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "About", "nav_order": 5}, {"name": "contact", "title": "Contact Us | Finetune", "sections": ["contact-hero", "contact-form", "contact-info"], "in_footer": true, "in_header": true, "nav_label": "Contact", "nav_order": 6}], "needs_logo": true, "needs_images": true, "image_prompts": {"logo": "A modern, technical logo for an AI deployment company called Finetune. Use clean, precise geometric shapes suggesting precision and optimization, with a professional color palette of deep navy blue and electric blue accents. The design should convey technical expertise, reliability, and practical innovation without being overly abstract.", "hero_home": "A sophisticated, technical background featuring abstract neural network patterns and data flow visualizations in deep navy blue and electric blue tones. Include subtle geometric grid patterns and flowing connection 