of interconnected AI agents and data pipelines. Dark navy blue base with glowing electric blue connection lines forming a subtle network pattern. The atmosphere should be sophisticated and engineering-focused, suggesting complex systems working in harmony. Include subtle geometric elements that imply automation and workflow orchestration."}, "style_collection": "professional-dark"}, "response_status": "complete", "response_received_at": "2026-03-20T02:01:41Z"}	pageflow-builder	site-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-03-20 02:01:54.086387+00	2026-03-20 12:40:03.053729+00	site-planner	f
d606ebd1-de0d-44de-b1ad-d26fb5345e47	15a6cb16-5a86-4541-a8e4-d7106239b6a4	tools	{"reasoning": "GameDesign.uk serves game developers and designers who need practical calculation tools for game systems design. Their existing blog content covers progression curves, combat balance, loot probability, and economy design — all of which have real mathematical underpinnings that benefit from interactive calculators. Custom tools are needed because none of the library tools address game design mathematics. The audience is technical and would genuinely use tools that help them balance numbers, model probability, and tune systems without writing code from scratch.", "suggestions": [{"name": "Loot Drop Probability Calculator", "function": "tool-loot-probability-calculator", "priority": 1, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Calculates the probability of obtaining at least one drop within N attempts given a base drop rate, supports pity timers and guaranteed drop thresholds. Directly complements the existing loot systems blog post and lets designers validate their drop tables without manual binomial calculations.", "target_page": "tools", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Progression Curve Builder", "function": "tool-progression-curve-builder", "priority": 2, "complexity": "moderate", "description": "Interactive calculator that plots XP or stat progression curves using exponential, polynomial, or linear models. Users input level count, starting value, and growth rate/exponent, and see a visual curve with a data table. Directly tied to the balancing progression curves blog post and is exactly the kind of tool game designers reach for when tuning level gates.", "target_page": "tools", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Combat Damage & TTK Calculator", "function": "tool-combat-ttk-calculator", "priority": 3, "complexity": "moderate", "description": "Time-to-kill calculator that takes attacker DPS, defender HP, armour/damage reduction, and crit rate/multiplier as inputs and outputs mean TTK, variance, and a probability distribution of kill times. Directly supports the health points blog post and helps designers validate combat feel before implementation.", "target_page": "tools", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Game Economy Inflation Simulator", "function": "tool-economy-inflation-simulator", "priority": 4, "complexity": "moderate", "description": "Models currency inflation over time given configurable gold sources (quests, drops, crafting) versus sinks (shop costs, repair fees, taxes). Shows equilibrium or runaway inflation curves. Directly extends the live game economy collapse blog post into an interactive tool designers can use to stress-test their economy designs.", "target_page": "tools", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Bayesian Rating Calculator", "function": "tool-bayesian-ranking", "priority": 5, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Demonstrates why naive average ratings for game features or items are misleading with small sample sizes. Could be repurposed for playtester feedback scoring or community rating systems — a genuine concern for indie developers managing early access feedback.", "target_page": "tools", "library_source": "tool-bayesian-ranking", "tool_component_id": "c345a76a-2c46-42b7-be16-1e34b4b19594"}], "rejected_tools": [{"reason": "A/B test significance is a marketing analytics tool. While game studios do run A/B tests, this audience is focused on systems design and balance math, not conversion rate optimisation.", "function": "tool-ab-test-calculator"}, {"reason": "Midjourney prompt builder is for visual content creation, not game systems design or balance. Not relevant to this audience's core needs.", "function": "tool-prompt-architect"}, {"reason": "Financial product for property finance. Completely irrelevant to game development.", "function": "tool-bridging-loan-calculator"}, {"reason": "Buy-to-let property investment tool. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-btl-investor"}, {"reason": "Property finance tool. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-equity-release"}, {"reason": "Fleet fuel purchasing tool. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-fuel-cost-estimator"}, {"reason": "Energy unit conversion for gas purchasing. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-gas-unit-converter"}, {"reason": "Industrial robotics engineering tool. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-gripper-payload-calculator"}, {"reason": "Image editing utility. While game developers use art tools, this is a generic utility with no connection to game systems design or the site's educational focus.", "function": "tool-bg-remover"}, {"reason": "Entertainment tool with no professional or educational value for game designers.", "function": "tool-meme-generator"}, {"reason": "UK mortgage product. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-mortgage-affordability"}, {"reason": "UK mortgage product. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-mortgage-overpayment"}, {"reason": "UK mortgage product. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-mortgage-repayment"}, {"reason": "Cybersecurity tool. While tangentially technical, password strength has no bearing on game systems design or balance.", "function": "tool-password-entropy"}, {"reason": "Web development utility. Not related to game design theory, systems, or balance — the core focus of this site.", "function": "tool-favicon-generator"}, {"reason": "UK property tax calculator. No relevance to game design.", "function": "tool-stamp-duty-calculator"}]}	tool-suggester	tool-suggester	\N	LLM tool evaluation — reasoning, recommendations, and rejections	t	2026-04-03 10:51:30.932618+00	\N	tool-suggester	f
c32b476f-8d8b-47a0-8c2d-9708bb715a4e	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	tools	{"reasoning": "Spark is a competitive opinion gaming platform targeting opinionated 18-35 year olds. The core value proposition is around archetypes, takes, and competitive engagement. The most useful tools would be things that deepen engagement with the archetype system, help users understand their play style, or create shareable content from their results. The library is heavily weighted toward finance and technical tools with almost no overlap. The Meme Studio is the only library tool with any plausible fit — users sharing takes and competing on provocations might want to create shareable meme content around their archetype or winning takes. The Bayesian Ranking Calculator could theoretically apply to scoring transparency but is too technical and abstract for this audience. Custom tools around archetype discovery, take scoring preview, or arena matchmaking would be far more relevant. However, even the Meme Studio is a stretch — Spark already has its own content creation loop (Stage Mode, Arena Mode) and adding a generic meme tool risks feeling off-brand. The most genuinely useful custom tool would be an Archetype Quiz Preview that lets visitors get a taste of the Daily Gauntlet experience before signing up — directly serving the conversion goal and the core product mechanic. A second useful tool would be a Provocation Rater that lets users preview how their take might score, reinforcing the competitive angle. These are lightweight, on-brand, and serve real pre-signup discovery needs.", "suggestions": [{"name": "Archetype Taster Quiz", "function": "tool-archetype-taster-quiz", "priority": 1, "complexity": "medium", "description": "A condensed 3-question version of the Daily Gauntlet experience that gives visitors a provisional archetype result before they sign up. Each question presents a provocation with multiple take options; the tool scores responses and reveals one of the 8 archetypes with a shareable result card. Directly serves conversion on the index and archetypes pages by letting visitors experience the core loop without committing to registration.", "target_page": "archetypes", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Take Scorer", "function": "tool-take-scorer", "priority": 2, "complexity": "medium", "description": "A lightweight tool where a visitor types in their take on a sample provocation and the AI-style scorer gives it a rating across dimensions like Originality, Heat, and Clarity — mimicking the Arena Mode scoring system. Builds curiosity about the full platform and demonstrates what competitive scoring feels like. Best placed on the gauntlet or provocations page to convert browsers into registered players.", "target_page": "gauntlet", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Meme Studio", "function": "tool-meme-generator", "priority": 3, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Client-side meme creator that lets users overlay text on images. Could allow players to turn their archetype result or a winning take into a shareable meme card. Marginally useful for virality and social sharing of results, though Spark's own Stage Mode partially overlaps this function.", "target_page": "archetypes", "library_source": "tool-meme-generator", "tool_component_id": "6ae53f32-be86-4c29-bc52-983c35d23b18"}], "rejected_tools": [{"reason": "Designed for marketers analysing conversion experiments. Spark's visitors are players and cultural consumers, not analytics professionals.", "function": "tool-ab-test-calculator"}, {"reason": "Too abstract and technical for an entertainment audience. While Spark uses scoring mechanics, visitors have no need to calculate Bayesian averages themselves.", "function": "tool-bayesian-ranking"}, {"reason": "Midjourney prompt builder for AI image generation. Irrelevant to opinion gaming and competitive takes.", "function": "tool-prompt-architect"}, {"reason": "Designed for game designers validating drop tables, not players on a social opinion platform. Spark has no loot or drop mechanics.", "function": "tool-loot-probability-calculator"}, {"reason": "Cybersecurity tool with no relevance to entertainment or social gaming.", "function": "tool-password-entropy"}, {"reason": "Developer utility. No relevance to Spark's end users.", "function": "tool-favicon-generator"}, {"reason": "Image editing utility. Not relevant to the opinion gaming context or visitor needs.", "function": "tool-bg-remover"}, {"reason": "Finance tool entirely unrelated to digital entertainment.", "function": "tool-mortgage-affordability"}, {"reason": "Finance tool entirely unrelated to digital entertainment.", "function": "tool-mortgage-repayment"}, {"reason": "Finance tool entirely unrelated to digital entertainment.", "function": "tool-mortgage-overpayment"}, {"reason": "UK property tax tool with no relevance to this platform or audience.", "function": "tool-stamp-duty-calculator"}, {"reason": "Specialist finance tool for property investors. Completely off-domain.", "function": "tool-bridging-loan-calculator"}, {"reason": "Buy-to-let property calculator. No relevance to social gaming.", "function": "tool-btl-investor"}, {"reason": "Finance tool for older homeowners. Misaligned with the 18-35 entertainment audience.", "function": "tool-equity-release"}, {"reason": "Fleet fuel management tool. Entirely unrelated industry.", "function": "tool-fuel-cost-estimator"}, {"reason": "Energy measurement utility. No relevance to opinion gaming.", "function": "tool-gas-unit-converter"}, {"reason": "Industrial robotics engineering tool. Completely unrelated to this platform.", "function": "tool-gripper-payload-calculator"}]}	tool-suggester	tool-suggester	\N	LLM tool evaluation — reasoning, recommendations, and rejections	f	2026-04-03 13:48:57.181765+00	2026-04-03 14:35:06.202747+00	tool-suggester	f
583ebc18-a7d1-49c1-ba54-821dcd58b675	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	tools	{"reasoning": "Spark is a competitive opinion gaming platform targeting opinionated 18-35 year olds. The core value proposition is around identity, competition, and cultural engagement. The Archetype Taster Quiz is already deployed and directly serves conversion. Beyond that, the most valuable tools would deepen engagement with the archetype/identity system, help users understand competitive scoring mechanics, or support the social/shareable nature of the platform. The library is heavily weighted toward finance, real estate, and technical tools — almost none of which are relevant here. Two custom tools stand out as genuinely useful: a provocation difficulty or 'heat score' rater that lets visitors gauge how spicy a take is before submitting, and an archetype compatibility tool that shows how two archetypes clash or align in Arena mode. The Meme Studio is a borderline case — the audience is culturally engaged and meme-literate, and shareable content is core to the platform, but meme creation is a feature Spark itself should build natively rather than outsource to a generic tool. The Loot Drop Probability Calculator has marginal relevance to game designers thinking about scoring systems but is not relevant to Spark's end users.", "suggestions": [{"name": "Archetype Clash Calculator", "function": "tool-archetype-clash-calculator", "priority": 1, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Lets a visitor select two archetypes and see a breakdown of how they typically match up in Arena Mode — who tends to dominate, what scoring patterns emerge, and what the rivalry dynamic looks like. Reinforces the competitive identity system, gives archetypes pages more depth, and creates a shareable social hook ('I'm a Contrarian vs your Hype Machine — here's why I win').", "target_page": "archetypes", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "Take Heat Scorer", "function": "tool-take-heat-scorer", "priority": 2, "complexity": "simple", "description": "A lightweight tool where a visitor types or pastes a take (opinion) and receives an AI-style 'heat score' based on heuristics — specificity, controversy, cultural relevance, originality. Gives visitors a taste of how Spark's scoring logic works before they sign up, directly supporting conversion on the gauntlet and provocations pages. Could also serve as a teaser for Arena Mode scoring.", "target_page": "gauntlet", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}], "rejected_tools": [{"reason": "The audience is meme-literate and shareable content matters, but a generic meme studio is not aligned with Spark's brand — it would feel like a detour from the competitive opinion loop rather than an extension of it. Spark should build native share cards, not point users to a generic tool.", "function": "tool-meme-generator"}, {"reason": "Relevant to game designers validating drop tables, not to Spark's end users who are opinionated cultural participants, not game mechanics engineers.", "function": "tool-loot-probability-calculator"}, {"reason": "Intended for marketers and analysts. Spark's visitors are players and cultural consumers, not conversion rate optimisers.", "function": "tool-ab-test-calculator"}, {"reason": "Midjourney-style prompt builder has no connection to opinion gaming or competitive takes.", "function": "tool-prompt-architect"}, {"reason": "Cybersecurity tool with no relevance to this platform or its audience.", "function": "tool-password-entropy"}, {"reason": "Developer utility. Not relevant to Spark's end users.", "function": "tool-favicon-generator"}, {"reason": "Image editing utility. Not relevant to competitive opinion gaming.", "function": "tool-bg-remover"}, {"reason": "Interesting conceptually given Spark's scoring system, but this is a data science explainer tool aimed at analysts, not a natural fit for 18-35 cultural gamers.", "function": "tool-bayesian-ranking"}, {"reason": "Finance tool. Entirely irrelevant to this audience and platform.", "function": "tool-mortgage-affordability"}, {"reason": "UK property tax tool. No relevance to digital entertainment platform.", "function": "tool-stamp-duty-calculator"}, {"reason": "Finance tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-mortgage-repayment"}, {"reason": "Finance tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-mortgage-overpayment"}, {"reason": "Finance tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-bridging-loan-calculator"}, {"reason": "Property investment tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-btl-investor"}, {"reason": "Finance tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-equity-release"}, {"reason": "Fleet fuel logistics tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-fuel-cost-estimator"}, {"reason": "Energy measurement tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-gas-unit-converter"}, {"reason": "Industrial robotics tool. No relevance.", "function": "tool-gripper-payload-calculator"}]}	tool-suggester	tool-suggester	\N	LLM tool evaluation — reasoning, recommendations, and rejections	t	2026-04-03 14:35:06.202747+00	\N	tool-suggester	f
3f1dcffa-d1ed-4e94-8798-080098a6669c	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	tools	{"reasoning": "FineTuning serves UK SME owners who are sceptical of AI hype and want concrete numbers before committing. The single most valuable tool is one that translates their current manual workload into a real savings estimate — giving them a tangible figure to justify internal budget conversations. The AI Agent ROI Estimator from the library is a near-perfect fit: it outputs time-to-ROI, annual savings, and FTE equivalent freed, which maps directly to what a non-technical SME owner needs to see. A secondary custom tool — an AI Readiness Quiz — would help visitors self-qualify and get a personalised recommendation, which suits the audience's scepticism and preference for honest, practical guidance before they contact anyone. The existing password entropy tool is already deployed and unrelated to the core audience need.", "suggestions": [{"name": "AI Time Savings Estimator", "function": "tool-ai-agent-roi-estimator", "priority": 1, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Lets SME owners input how many hours per week their team spends on repetitive tasks (email triage, data entry, scheduling, reporting etc.), their rough staff cost, and current error rates. Outputs estimated annual cost of doing it manually vs. post-AI, projected annual saving, and FTE equivalent freed. Gives the visitor a concrete number to take into an internal conversation — directly addressing the 'is it worth it for a business my size?' question that blocks most SME decisions.", "target_page": "ai-for-uk-small-business", "library_source": "tool-ai-agent-roi-estimator", "tool_component_id": "fb58cdde-d809-4005-a15a-644d1a334db8"}, {"name": "AI Readiness Quiz", "function": "tool-ai-readiness-quiz", "priority": 2, "complexity": "simple", "description": "A short 5–7 question quiz asking about business size, industry, current pain points (e.g. admin overload, slow customer responses, manual reporting), existing software stack, and appetite for change. Outputs a plain-English readiness score and a personalised summary of where AI is most likely to help — or an honest note that they may not be ready yet. Builds trust with sceptical visitors and acts as a soft lead qualifier before they reach the contact page.", "target_page": "ai-for-your-type-of-business", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}, {"name": "AI Prompt Builder for Business Tasks", "function": "tool-business-prompt-builder", "priority": 3, "complexity": "simple", "description": "A structured form where visitors select a business task (e.g. write a customer email, summarise a meeting, draft a job ad, create a report), fill in a few context fields, and get a ready-to-use prompt for ChatGPT or similar. Complements the existing blog post on writing useful AI prompts and gives non-technical visitors an immediate, tangible win — reinforcing FineTuning's practical, no-jargon positioning.", "target_page": "how-to-write-a-useful-ai-prompt-for-business-tasks", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}], "rejected_tools": [{"reason": "Visitors are SME owners evaluating AI adoption, not marketers running conversion experiments. Irrelevant to their decision-making context.", "function": "tool-ab-test-calculator"}, {"reason": "Designed for Midjourney-style image prompts with lighting and camera toggles. Not useful for business task prompting and would confuse a non-technical SME audience.", "function": "tool-prompt-architect"}, {"reason": "Built for a gamified personality/archetype product. Has no relevance to AI consulting for UK SMEs.", "function": "tool-archetype-taster-quiz"}, {"reason": "A statistics demonstration tool. Interesting but has no practical application for SME owners evaluating AI services.", "function": "tool-bayesian-ranking"}, {"reason": "Finance product tool for property transactions. Completely outside this site's domain.", "function": "tool-bridging-loan-calculator"}, {"reason": "Buy-to-let property investment tool. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-btl-investor"}, {"reason": "Property finance tool. Not relevant to this audience or industry.", "function": "tool-equity-release"}, {"reason": "Designed for fleet managers and fuel buyers. No relevance to AI consulting for SMEs.", "function": "tool-fuel-cost-estimator"}, {"reason": "Energy industry utility. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-gas-unit-converter"}, {"reason": "Industrial robotics engineering tool. Completely outside this site's scope.", "function": "tool-gripper-payload-calculator"}, {"reason": "Game design tool for loot drop mechanics. Not relevant to UK SME AI consulting.", "function": "tool-loot-probability-calculator"}, {"reason": "Image editing utility. Not relevant to the site's purpose or audience needs.", "function": "tool-bg-remover"}, {"reason": "Inappropriate for a professional B2B AI consulting site targeting sceptical business owners.", "function": "tool-meme-generator"}, {"reason": "Mortgage product tool. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-mortgage-affordability"}, {"reason": "Mortgage product tool. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-mortgage-overpayment"}, {"reason": "Mortgage product tool. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-mortgage-repayment"}, {"reason": "Web development utility. Not relevant to SME owners evaluating AI services.", "function": "tool-favicon-generator"}, {"reason": "UK property tax calculator. Not relevant to AI consulting.", "function": "tool-stamp-duty-calculator"}]}	tool-suggester	tool-suggester	\N	LLM tool evaluation — reasoning, recommendations, and rejections	t	2026-04-04 06:03:19.099911+00	\N	tool-suggester	f
db1f85df-39ac-487e-bf39-bb253472dbcc	4851f6fc-71cf-4160-a270-e03d6d3e0732	tools	{"reasoning": "Leopardess Consulting's audience is CTOs, engineering leads, and technical founders at UK scale-ups and B2B SaaS companies. These visitors evaluate vendors on production credibility and delivery track record. The most valuable tools are those that help decision-makers quantify the business case for AI automation internally — giving them concrete numbers to take into budget conversations — and tools that help them self-assess readiness. The AI Agent ROI Estimator is a near-perfect fit: it maps directly to the Multi-Agent Systems and Digital Transformation Strategy services and produces the kind of output a CTO can paste into a board deck. The AI Readiness Quiz is also a strong fit as a soft lead qualifier for technically-literate buyers who are sceptical and want to self-assess before committing to a conversation. A custom Agent Complexity Estimator could also serve this audience well by letting engineering leads scope out what kind of multi-agent architecture their use case might require. The password entropy tool already deployed is mildly relevant as a technical credibility signal but is not a core conversion driver.", "suggestions": [{"name": "AI Agent ROI Estimator", "function": "tool-ai-agent-roi-estimator", "priority": 1, "complexity": "simple", "description": "Lets CTOs and engineering leads input current workflow details — manual steps, team hours per week, average salary, error rate — and receive estimated annual cost of manual operations vs. projected cost post-automation. Outputs time-to-ROI, annual savings, and FTE equivalent freed. Gives decision-makers a concrete number to take into internal budget conversations and directly supports the Multi-Agent Systems and Digital Transformation Strategy services.", "target_page": "services", "library_source": "tool-ai-agent-roi-estimator", "tool_component_id": "fb58cdde-d809-4005-a15a-644d1a334db8"}, {"name": "AI Readiness Quiz", "function": "tool-ai-readiness-quiz", "priority": 2, "complexity": "simple", "description": "A 5–7 question quiz asking about business size, current pain points, existing stack, and appetite for change. Outputs a plain-English readiness score and personalised summary of where AI agent automation is most likely to help. Acts as a soft lead qualifier for technically-literate but sceptical buyers before they reach the contact page — builds trust by being honest about fit rather than overselling.", "target_page": "how-it-works", "library_source": "tool-ai-readiness-quiz", "tool_component_id": "a39145ce-8d95-4dc6-a151-7282bb0a23a5"}, {"name": "Agent Architecture Complexity Estimator", "function": "tool-agent-complexity-estimator", "priority": 3, "complexity": "simple", "description": "A custom tool where engineering leads describe their target workflow: number of distinct task types, required integrations (APIs, databases, queues), expected concurrency, and whether stateful memory is needed. The tool outputs a rough architecture tier (single agent, supervisor-worker, full hierarchical mesh) with a plain-English rationale, indicative stack components (e.g. Kafka for async, Postgres for state, Kubernetes for orchestration), and a ballpark build complexity rating. Directly demonstrates Leopardess's stack depth and helps technical visitors self-qualify before booking a discovery call.", "target_page": "technical-architecture", "library_source": null, "tool_component_id": null}], "rejected_tools": [{"reason": "A/B test significance is a marketing analytics tool. Leopardess's audience is engineering leads and CTOs evaluating AI infrastructure vendors, not conversion rate optimisers.", "function": "tool-ab-test-calculator"}, {"reason": "Midjourney-style prompt builder is aimed at image generation users. Irrelevant to an AI agent orchestration consultancy targeting technical B2B buyers.", "function": "tool-prompt-architect"}, {"reason": "Built for a specific gamified 