57a81696-14cb-410f-af8f-b7010fdfa075	15a6cb16-5a86-4541-a8e4-d7106239b6a4	identity	{"tone": "Direct, authoritative, technical, and confident — written for practitioners rather than beginners", "tagline": "Design with Authority.", "industry": "Game Development / Game Design Education", "services": [{"name": "Tools & Calculators", "description": "Browser-based game design calculators for progression curves, combat balance, loot probability, and physics math"}, {"name": "Guides & Theory", "description": "Deep-dives into game design theory, systems thinking, and academic principles covering probability, psychology, economy design, and networking"}, {"name": "Interactive Games", "description": "Interactive prototypes that bring game design concepts to life, including AI pathfinding, network topology, game feel, and economy simulation"}], "adopted_at": "2026-04-03T08:51:48Z", "adopted_from": "gamedesign.uk", "company_name": "GameDesign.uk", "target_audience": "Game developers and designers seeking tools, theory, and interactive prototypes for systems, economy, and balance design", "hero_headline_canonical": "Model It Before You Build It. — This headline synthesises the empirical rigour implied by 'Design with Authority' and the action-orientation of 'Start Building. Stop Guessing.' It positions the site as a modelling and simulation layer that precedes production, which is accurate to the toolset (calculators, probability distributions, progression curve models). It carries the punchy declarative fragment style consistent with the established voice, avoids credential-claiming, and creates productive tension by implying the reader's current workflow skips the modelling step. All hero components across index, tool pages, and landing pages should reference this canonical value. The two competing variants should be retired."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-04-06 23:00:31.310348+00	2026-04-06 23:01:27.801035+00	content-gap-planner	f
47e3b558-5473-4998-8f83-e86f12703bfb	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	strategy	{"tone": "bold", "site_type": "landing-page", "domain_type": "company_brand", "growth_path": "V1 establishes the daily engagement loop and viral archetype sharing mechanic with zero infrastructure overhead via static S3. Growth is driven by Gauntlet completion rate and share rate — each shared archetype card is a distribution event that brings new players into the lobby. V2 introduces AI sparring and user accounts, converting anonymous Gauntlet players into registered users with persistent reputation and daily return incentive. V3 adds live challenge rooms and arena mode, creating the community layer that makes daily return habitual rather than occasional. V4 introduces Stage mode and monetisation, by which point behavioural archetype data enables genuine niche discovery and creator tools with real commercial value.", "search_intent": {"primary_intent": "navigational", "likely_searches": ["vonc", "vonc.com", "spark social platform", "spark opinion game", "daily gauntlet quiz", "archetype quiz", "AI opinion game platform", "spark daily gauntlet"], "high_value_terms": ["spark social platform", "daily gauntlet archetype quiz", "opinion game platform", "AI social platform game"]}, "revenue_models": {"affiliate": {"fit": "poor_fit", "reasoning": "No product category or purchasing context exists. Affiliate links would break the game-energy aesthetic and distract from the platform engagement loop that drives all value."}, "saas_tools": {"fit": "possible", "reasoning": "The Daily Gauntlet and archetype system function as interactive tools. Future versions could introduce paid tiers for deeper analytics, reputation tracking, or creator tools — making a freemium SaaS layer plausible in v3 or v4 once behavioural data is established."}, "primary_model": "direct_business", "direct_business": {"fit": "strong_fit", "reasoning": "The site IS the product. Revenue paths are embedded in the platform itself — future premium features, creator tools, brand partnerships, and Stage mode marketplace all flow from the direct business model. V1 establishes the engagement loop that all future monetisation depends on."}, "lead_generation": {"fit": "poor_fit", "reasoning": "This is a consumer platform, not a B2B lead capture context. There are no third-party businesses to sell leads to and the engagement loop is entirely self-contained."}, "secondary_models": ["saas_tools"], "sponsored_listings": {"fit": "poor_fit", "reasoning": "No directory or listing structure exists or is planned. Entirely irrelevant to this platform model."}, "display_advertising": {"fit": "possible", "reasoning": "Once daily active users scale, display or native advertising could be introduced. However it is premature for v1 and the dark game-arena aesthetic conflicts with standard display ad formats. A future consideration only."}}, "content_strategy": "Content is the product. Daily provocations pulled from real-world events serve dual purpose: they are the game material and the SEO content engine. Each provocation page is a shareable, indexable unit that builds topical relevance over time. The Daily Gauntlet drives return visits and social sharing through archetype cards — visitors share results, new visitors encounter the provocation card and enter the loop. The archetypes page provides evergreen content that captures search traffic from people who received a shared card and want to understand their archetype. The about page handles platform comparison searches. No long-form editorial content in v1 — the game is the depth, the interface is the explanation, and copy exists only to get the visitor into the experience as fast as possible.", "value_proposition": "Spark is the daily game where your opinion is the entry point — real-world provocations, timed takes, and a behaviour-earned identity that reveals who you actually are when the stakes are real.", "site_type_reasoning": "The explicit strategic directive is that the product IS the landing page. V1 is a content-first static site designed to drive engagement immediately — a single provocation card fills the screen, the text input is the first interaction, no signup wall exists. This is not a brochure presenting a business, nor an authority portal building category SEO traffic. Every page serves a single conversion goal: get the visitor to engage, complete the Gauntlet, and share their archetype card. The Daily Gauntlet and archetype quiz are viral acquisition mechanics embedded in the site itself. The provocations feed doubles as SEO content but its primary function is game surface, not editorial publishing. This is landing-page strategy executed across a 5-page structure where each page is either a game interface or a gateway into one.", "competitive_position": {"defensible_moat": "The archetype system is earned through behaviour rather than self-reported, making it genuinely novel and difficult to replicate without rebuilding the entire engagement model. The Daily Gauntlet creates a daily return habit loop that feeds the identity system. AI positioned as game master rather than performer is a structural choice that competitors would have to fundamentally reorient their content models to replicate. Ephemeral challenges producing permanent emergent reputation is architecturally distinct from every major incumbent.", "gap_opportunity": "No platform currently combines real-time cultural provocation, competitive opinion play, and a behaviour-emergent identity system in a single daily game format. The gap is the intersection of game mechanics, opinion expression, and ephemeral challenge rooms — none of the incumbents occupy this space. The Daily Gauntlet has no direct competitor as a daily opinion game that produces a shareable identity artefact.", "current_landscape": "The social platform space is dominated by TikTok (passive consumption), Twitter/X (broadcast and argument), and Reddit (karma-hierarchical permanence). Daily game formats exist via Wordle and NYT Games but lack opinion expression or identity mechanics. Archetype and quiz tools like BuzzFeed and 16Personalities lack real-time cultural relevance or competitive framing. No major platform occupies the intersection of game mechanics, opinion expression, and behavioural identity."}, "domain_type_reasoning": "VONC is a short, coined 4-letter domain with no generic industry meaning, no geographic component, and no product category association. It functions purely as a brand identifier. The research confirms it is being used as the technical host for Spark, a specific AI-driven social platform product. The domain has no standalone search value as a category term — its value is entirely in the brand being built on top of it.", "recommended_page_types": [{"page_type": "index", "reasoning": "The home page is the primary acquisition surface and must be treated as its own distinct experience — a single provocation card filling the viewport, a text input, a timer, a lobby grid of active provocations, and a Gauntlet CTA. It is architecturally distinct from all other pages and must load with daily-refreshed content. It is the first impression and the product simultaneously."}, {"page_type": "tool", "reasoning": "The Daily Gauntlet is a fully functional client-side interactive tool — 5 timed provocations, scored responses, archetype generation, and shareable card output. It requires state management, JS interaction, and a result output surface. The provocation cards also have tool-like properties with shareable individual URLs. These are the viral acquisition mechanics of the entire platform."}, {"page_type": "blog-index", "reasoning": "The provocations feed functions as the blog-index equivalent — a daily-updated card-based listing of active provocations, each with its own shareable URL. This is the SEO content engine of v1, building topical relevance to real-world events over time while simultaneously serving as live game surface."}, {"page_type": "blog-post", "reasoning": "Each individual provocation has its own shareable URL and functions as an indexable SEO content unit — a game card with a cultural hook, an AI-framed question, and a response prompt. These accumulate as organic search traffic over time as a secondary benefit of the daily generation loop."}, {"page_type": "content", "reasoning": "The about page and archetypes page are content pages that explain the platform, the game metaphor, and the archetype system. They serve visitors who arrive via shared archetype cards and need context, support SEO for platform comparison searches, and convert curious visitors into Gauntlet participants via terminal CTAs."}, {"page_type": "landing", "reasoning": "The about page functions as a secondary conversion landing page with a Gauntlet CTA as its terminal action. It handles platform comparison searches and positions Spark against TikTok, Twitter, and Reddit with a single conversion goal: get the visitor into the Gauntlet."}]}	domain-strategist	domain-strategist	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 11:02:01.656134+00	\N	domain-strategist	f
b8717786-4cbf-4df8-9a48-346f134866c9	1368e337-dd1d-4799-bbb3-8221a1b79bcc	briefing	{"tagline": "From idea to AI system", "about_us": "  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our aim is to make AI genuinely useful.   ## AI systems that actually do the work  Most companies experimenting with AI end up with prototypes, demos, or chatbots.  Very few end up with systems that **save time, automate work, or generate measurable value**.  Finetune helps organisations design and deploy practical AI systems — automation pipelines, specialised models, and intelligent agents that solve real operational problems.  Not AI theatre.  ---  Real systems.  # Rapid experimentation  AI technology is moving quickly.  The companies that benefit most are those that can **experiment cheaply and deploy quickly**.  We aim to make it easy to test ideas, build prototypes, and evolve them into real systems when they prove useful.   ---  # What we build  We work with companies to build AI infrastructure that fits into real workflows.  ### Automation systems  AI that screens requests, processes documents, extracts information, and routes work automatically.  ### Intelligent agent pipelines  Systems where multiple AI agents collaborate to solve problems, analyse information, or complete complex tasks.  ### Custom AI models  Fine-tuned models trained on domain-specific data using techniques such as LoRA and other efficient training methods.  ### RAG systems for company knowledge  AI that can search and reason over internal data such as documents, emails, financial information, and knowledge bases.  ### Private AI deployments  Secure systems where models can run locally or within controlled environments to protect sensitive data.  ### Data collection infrastructure  Large-scale web data pipelines capable of gathering structured information from thousands of sources.  ---  # Why most AI projects fail  Many AI initiatives stall for predictable reasons.  **They start with tools instead of problems.**  **They stay in prototype mode.**  **They rely on third-party systems that can’t integrate with existing workflows.**  **Or they assume a single AI model will magically solve everything.**  In practice, useful AI systems usually require:  * data pipelines * automation layers * model adaptation * monitoring and iteration  AI works best as **part of a system**, not as a standalone tool.  ---  # The Finetune approach  We focus on **practical deployment**.  That means starting with a real operational problem and designing a system around it.  A typical project might involve:  1. Collecting and structuring the relevant data 2. Building automation pipelines 3. Training or adapting models 4. Integrating the system into existing workflows 5. Iterating until the system reliably saves time or improves decisions  The goal is not simply to use AI.  The goal is to make something **genuinely useful**.  ---  # What we can help with  Examples of problems we help solve:  * Screening and routing incoming requests * Automating quoting or proposal workflows * Extracting structured information from documents * Building internal knowledge assistants * Collecting market or financial data at scale * Deploying private AI models for sensitive workflows * Setting up agent pipelines that can perform complex multi-step tasks  Some systems are simple and highly targeted.  Others involve networks of cooperating agents and large-scale data pipelines.  ---  # A note on scale  We are particularly interested in **agent systems and large-scale automation**.  This includes experimentation with environments where thousands of AI agents can communicate and collaborate to solve problems.  These systems are still emerging, but they point toward a future where much of the routine work inside organisations can be handled by coordinated software agents.  Our goal is to help companies begin exploring that future in a practical way.  ---    ---  # Who we work with  We tend to work best with organisations that:  * have complex workflows or data * are open to experimentation * want to build internal capability with AI rather than just outsource it  This includes startups, established companies, and technical teams exploring new ways to operate.  ---  # About Finetune  Finetune is a small technical company focused on practical AI deployment.  We build systems that combine automation, data pipelines, model training, and agent-based architectures.  Our focus is simple:  **make AI genuinely useful inside real organisations.**  ---  # Call to action  ## Curious what AI could automate in your business?  We’re always happy to have a technical conversation about possible approaches.  Contact us to discuss your workflows, data, or ideas.", "services": [{"name": "AI Automation Systems  ", "description": "Design and deployment of AI-driven automation pipelines that remove manual work from business processes. Examples include request screening, automated quoting, document analysis, and workflow orchestration."}, {"name": "Intelligent Agent Systems", "description": "Design and deployment of networks of AI agents capable of solving complex tasks collaboratively. These systems can analyse information, communicate with each other, and perform large-scale problem solving. Talk to us about systems capable of running tens of thousands of AI agents communicating with each other to solve complex tasks."}, {"name": "Custom AI Model Training", "description": "Training specialised models using techniques such as LoRA, DoRA, and other parameter-efficient methods to adapt modern AI models to your company's specific needs."}, {"name": "RAG Systems for Company Data", "description": "Deployment of Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems that allow AI to search and reason over your internal data including:  Emails  Documents  Financial records  Marketing material  Knowledge bases"}, {"name": "Bulk Data Collection", "description": "Large-scale web data extraction across thousands of websites, including structured business and financial data collection."}, {"name": "Financial and Company Data Pipelines", "description": "Automated systems for collecting and analysing financial data from public sources including company registries and regulatory filings."}, {"name": "Private AI Deployments", "description": "Secure deployment of AI systems that run privately — including models that can run locally or in-browser to protect company data and reduce usage costs."}, {"name": "Agent Pipeline Infrastructure", "description": "Installation and configuration of agent frameworks and orchestration systems so companies can run their own AI agents in production."}, {"name": "Rapid Website Generation", "description": "Creation of complex, high-quality static websites within minutes for:  company identity  marketing pages  landing pages  documentation  presentations"}, {"name": "AI Strategy & Implementation", "description": "Hands-on support helping companies move from curiosity about AI to systems that actually work inside their business."}, {"name": "High-Volume Data Acquisition", "description": "Design systems capable of collecting structured information from thousands of websites automatically."}], "company_name": "FineTuning"}	pageflow-builder	briefing-agent	\N	\N	t	2026-03-21 14:41:28.346374+00	\N	briefing-agent	f
