26608664-8364-4190-968b-92bcb5678dbf	15a6cb16-5a86-4541-a8e4-d7106239b6a4	identity	{"tone": "Direct, authoritative, technical, and confident — written for practitioners rather than beginners", "tagline": "Design with Authority.", "industry": "Game Development / Game Design Education", "services": [{"name": "Tools & Calculators", "description": "Browser-based game design calculators for progression curves, combat balance, loot probability, and physics math"}, {"name": "Guides & Theory", "description": "Deep-dives into game design theory, systems thinking, and academic principles covering probability, psychology, economy design, and networking"}, {"name": "Interactive Games", "description": "Interactive prototypes that bring game design concepts to life, including AI pathfinding, network topology, game feel, and economy simulation"}], "adopted_at": "2026-04-03T08:51:48Z", "adopted_from": "gamedesign.uk", "company_name": "GameDesign.uk", "target_audience": "Independent and mid-size studio game designers and systems designers who are past the beginner stage — they are building real games, managing real economies, and running real balance problems. They are comfortable with mathematics, frustrated by guesswork, and looking for rigorous tools and theory they can apply directly. Secondary audience: technically-minded students in game design programmes who are self-directed and seeking practitioner-level depth beyond what courses provide. Not targeting: casual hobbyists, non-technical producers, or enterprise AAA studios with dedicated internal tooling teams.", "hero_headline_canonical": "Model It Before You Build It. — This headline synthesises the empirical rigour implied by 'Design with Authority' and the action-orientation of 'Start Building. Stop Guessing.' It positions the site as a modelling and simulation layer that precedes production, which is accurate to the toolset (calculators, probability distributions, progression curve models). It carries the punchy declarative fragment style consistent with the established voice, avoids credential-claiming, and creates productive tension by implying the reader's current workflow skips the modelling step. All hero components across index, tool pages, and landing pages should reference this canonical value. The two competing variants should be retired."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-04-06 23:01:27.809074+00	2026-04-06 23:29:53.176317+00	content-gap-planner	f
