d70cd4da-11d0-45ad-8a45-4472c9ea8a05	2a8ebf9c-20a2-4c39-b191-840b012371da	identity	{"tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "agents@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": "Get production-ready websites up and running in minutes with our AI-powered multi-agent systems. We handle secure, scalable hosting on Cloudflare, including automated builds, testing, and launches – removing the usual hurdles so you can focus on what matters."}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": "We design custom hierarchical agent setups to address your business challenges. Supporting a range of LLMs and models, these systems delegate tasks sensibly, collaborate in real time, and scale smoothly for effective automation."}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": "Clear guidance to integrate AI and modern technology into your everyday operations. We work with you to build straightforward roadmaps for AI adoption, streamlining workflows, and staying agile in a fast-changing world."}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": "Practical advice on modern web architectures, smart deployment, and useful AI integrations. We help your team build solid, forward-thinking web applications that focus on speed, security, and real innovation."}], "company_name": "AI Agent Orchestration", "about_summary": "AI Agent Orchestration builds production-grade multi-agent systems on proven infrastructure — Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres. We design hierarchical agent architectures that automate complex workflows, from automated website deployment to real-time agent collaboration. No demos. No slide decks. Working systems, deployed and running.", "site_metadata": "industry: AI infrastructure and enterprise software; target_audience: CTOs, engineering leads, and technology decision-makers at mid-to-large enterprises and scaling startups evaluating or deploying AI agent systems in production — secondary audience includes startup founders and business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable outcomes; tone: technical, direct, and practitioner-led — written by builders for builders, not advisory or consultative in register; purpose: lead generation for custom AI agent build engagements, supported by authoritative technical content that establishes credibility with engineering decision-makers", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Primary: CTOs, VP Engineering, and engineering leads at mid-to-large enterprises (500+ employees) and scaling startups (Series B+) who are evaluating or actively deploying AI agent systems in production. They care about reliability at scale, observability, team handoff, compliance, and the real cost of failure — not theoretical AI potential. They are skeptical of hype, respect technical depth, and make decisions based on architecture quality and production track record. Secondary: startup founders and forward-thinking business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable ROI outcomes, who rely on engineering leadership to validate technical claims.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "target_audience_tone_purpose": "Target Audience: CTOs, engineering leads, VP Engineering, and technically sophisticated startup founders evaluating production AI infrastructure. Secondary: forward-thinking business owners who understand technology investment. Tone: Direct, confident, and technically credible — written by builders for builders. No fluff, no vague consulting language. Purpose: Lead generation and consultation bookings for AI agent orchestration engagements, supported by demonstration of deep technical competence through case studies, tooling, and blog content.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI infrastructure and enterprise automation. Target Audience: CTOs, engineering leads, and operations directors at mid-market to enterprise companies, plus scaling startup founders evaluating production AI agent deployments. Tone: confident, direct, and technically credible — written by builders for builders, not by consultants for executives. Purpose: generate qualified inbound leads for custom multi-agent system design and production deployment engagements.", "target_audience_tone_and_conversion_goals": "Primary audience: CTOs, VP Engineering, and senior engineering leads at Series B+ startups and mid-to-large enterprises who are actively evaluating or deploying AI agent systems in production. Secondary audience: startup founders and technically-literate business leaders seeking measurable AI automation outcomes. Tone: technical, direct, and peer-to-peer — written by engineers who build real systems, not consultants who theorize. Avoid marketing fluff; lead with architecture decisions, production tradeoffs, and concrete outcomes. Primary conversion goal: discovery call or contact form submission. Secondary goal: blog content engagement and return visits that build trust before outreach.", "industry,target_audience,tone,messaging_pillars": "industry: AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services. target_audience_primary: CTOs, VP Engineering, and engineering leads at mid-to-large enterprises and scaling startups who are evaluating or actively deploying AI agent systems in production — they are technical, skeptical of hype, and need production-grade answers not theoretical frameworks. target_audience_secondary: Startup founders and forward-thinking business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable business outcomes. tone: Direct, technically credible, practitioner-first — written by engineers who ship real systems, not consultants who produce slide decks. No hype, no vague promises. Concrete stack references (Kubernetes, Kafka, Postgres), real failure modes, and honest trade-offs. messaging_pillars: (1) Production reality over proof-of-concept theater — we build systems that survive contact with real workloads. (2) Orchestration as a first-class engineering discipline, not an afterthought. (3) Stack-specific expertise — opinionated choices grounded in operational experience. (4) Measurable outcomes — agent systems justified by business impact, not novelty."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-04-07 02:02:28.139865+00	2026-04-07 03:38:44.155647+00	content-gap-planner	f
a3331115-ef58-42b1-bbd1-4316729ec8e6	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	briefing	{"gaps": ["contact_phone", "headquarters", "leadership_team", "case_studies", "contact_email"], "tone": "bold", "tagline": "TikTok is where you watch. Twitter is where you shout. Spark is where you play.", "about_us": "Spark is an AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game. Not another social app. A daily game powered by what is happening in the world. You don't post. You don't scroll. You play.\\n\\nSpark positions itself at the intersection of game mechanics, opinion expression, and ephemeral challenge rooms. AI serves as game master and producer — it frames provocations, keeps score, curates content, and synthesises results. When something is funny or impressive, a human did it.\\n\\nThe platform combines Arena mode (competitive takes) and Stage mode (creative showcase) with a behavioural archetype system. Your profile emerges from how you engage, not from what you claim to be. Ephemeral challenges produce permanent emergent reputation.\\n\\nSpark is built for people with opinions on current trends but no platform that asks for them, creators wanting skill showcase with built-in audience, and curators who find things rather than make them.", "has_blog": false, "industry": "Social Platform / Interactive Media", "services": [{"name": "Daily Provocations", "description": "AI-generated provocations pulled from real-world events. Each provocation is a shareable card with a text input, timer, and AI take. The world provides the content — you provide the take."}, {"name": "Daily Gauntlet", "description": "5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. A client-side interactive quiz that mixes opinion and creation prompts, scored on response speed, originality, consistency, and topic preferences. Produces a shareable archetype card."}, {"name": "Archetype System", "description": "8 behavioural archetypes earned through engagement: The Surgeon, The Wildcard, The Oracle, The Catalyst, The Judge, The Maker, The Scout, The Mentor. Your profile emerges from how you play, not from self-reported traits."}, {"name": "Arena Mode", "description": "Competitive opinion space where takes are scored, compared, and synthesised. Enter a room with energy — don't scroll a stream. Engagement is guaranteed."}, {"name": "Stage Mode", "description": "Creative showcase space for skill demonstration. Built for makers who show up with creations, not opinions. Niche discovery through consistent output."}], "site_type": "landing-page", "has_careers": false, "case_studies": null, "company_name": "VONC", "headquarters": null, "contact_email": "[INFERRED] hello@vonc.com", "contact_phone": null, "leadership_team": null, "briefing_confidence": 0.92, "recommended_builder": "pageflow-builder"}	build-briefing-agent	build-briefing-agent	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 11:43:47.131521+00	\N	build-briefing-agent	f
