a2872eb5-f1e6-4006-8f2e-4d7063687865	15a6cb16-5a86-4541-a8e4-d7106239b6a4	identity	{"tone": "Direct, authoritative, technical, and confident — written for practitioners rather than beginners", "tagline": "Design with Authority.", "industry": "Game Development / Game Design Education", "services": [{"name": "Tools & Calculators", "description": "Browser-based game design calculators for progression curves, combat balance, loot probability, and physics math"}, {"name": "Guides & Theory", "description": "Deep-dives into game design theory, systems thinking, and academic principles covering probability, psychology, economy design, and networking"}, {"name": "Interactive Games", "description": "Interactive prototypes that bring game design concepts to life, including AI pathfinding, network topology, game feel, and economy simulation"}], "adopted_at": "2026-04-03T08:51:48Z", "adopted_from": "gamedesign.uk", "company_name": "GameDesign.uk", "site_metadata": "Tagline: Rigorous tools and theory for game designers who build real systems. Purpose: GameDesign.uk provides mathematically grounded tools, calculators, and practitioner-level guides for independent and mid-size studio game designers solving real balance, economy, and systems design problems. Target audience: Independent and mid-size studio game designers and systems designers past the beginner stage — comfortable with mathematics, building real games, managing live economies, and seeking rigorous directly applicable methodology over guesswork. Tone: Formal-technical with a sharp, confident edge — authoritative through demonstrated specificity, not claimed credentials; challenging and empowering; second person in CTAs, third person for systems and concepts, first person absent.", "target_audience": "Primary: Independent and mid-size studio game designers and systems designers who are past the beginner stage — building real games, managing real economies, and solving real balance problems. Comfortable with mathematics, frustrated by guesswork, seeking rigorous and directly applicable tools and theory. Secondary: Technically-minded game design students who are self-directed and seeking practitioner-level depth beyond course material. Excluded: casual hobbyists, non-technical producers, AAA studios with dedicated internal tooling teams.", "core_value_proposition": "Stop Guessing. Start Building. — The canonical headline and positioning statement for GameDesign.uk. Used consistently across all hero components, landing pages, and primary CTAs sitewide. Reflects the site's core promise: replacing guesswork and intuition-based design with rigorous, mathematically grounded tools and theory. Secondary tagline 'Design with Authority.' is retired and should not appear in new content.", "hero_headline_canonical": "Model It Before You Build It. — This headline synthesises the empirical rigour implied by 'Design with Authority' and the action-orientation of 'Start Building. Stop Guessing.' It positions the site as a modelling and simulation layer that precedes production, which is accurate to the toolset (calculators, probability distributions, progression curve models). It carries the punchy declarative fragment style consistent with the established voice, avoids credential-claiming, and creates productive tension by implying the reader's current workflow skips the modelling step. All hero components across index, tool pages, and landing pages should reference this canonical value. The two competing variants should be retired."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-04-07 02:09:35.507924+00	2026-04-07 03:22:33.972312+00	content-gap-planner	f
