 exclamation marks.", "site_metadata": "Tagline: Rigorous tools and theory for game designers who build real systems. Purpose: GameDesign.uk provides mathematically grounded tools, calculators, and practitioner-level guides for independent and mid-size studio game designers solving real balance, economy, and systems design problems. Target audience: Independent and mid-size studio game designers and systems designers past the beginner stage — comfortable with mathematics, building real games, managing live economies, and seeking rigorous directly applicable methodology over guesswork. Tone: Formal-technical with a sharp, confident edge — authoritative through demonstrated specificity, not claimed credentials; challenging and empowering; second person in CTAs, third person for systems and concepts, first person absent.", "target_audience": "Primary: Independent and mid-size studio game designers and systems designers who are past the beginner stage — building real games, managing real economies, and solving real balance problems. Comfortable with mathematics, frustrated by guesswork, seeking rigorous and directly applicable tools and theory. Secondary: Technically-minded game design students who are self-directed and seeking practitioner-level depth beyond course material. Excluded: casual hobbyists, non-technical producers, AAA studios with dedicated internal tooling teams.", "canonical_hero_copy": "Headline: 'Stop Guessing. Start Building.' — this is the primary value proposition headline for the homepage hero only. It is direct, provocative in the site's established register, and positions the site as a corrective force against guesswork, consistent with the emotional tone directive. Subheadline: 'Rigorous tools, models, and theory for game designers who build real systems and need them to work.' — this names the audience (designers building real systems), signals the methodology (rigorous tools and models), and excludes casual or beginner users implicitly. 'Design with Authority.' is retired as a headline variant and may be repurposed only as supporting copy or a section tagline if needed. Interior pages (contact, tools, guides) must not use the hero component — they should use page-specific, lower-hierarchy headers appropriate to their context.", "positioning_statement": "GameDesign.uk is a technical resource for independent and mid-size studio game designers who are past the beginner stage and need rigorous, mathematically grounded tools and theory to solve real balance, economy, and systems design problems. It exists to replace guesswork with method — offering calculators, models, and practitioner-level guides that AAA studios build internally and everyone else lacks. It is not a news site, a tutorial aggregator, or a beginner onboarding platform. Its nearest alternatives are GameDeveloper.com (broad, editorial, non-technical) and personal practitioner blogs (deep but fragmented and undiscoverable) — GameDesign.uk occupies the gap between them: structured, tool-first, and technically uncompromising.", "core_value_proposition": "Stop Guessing. Start Building. — The canonical headline and positioning statement for GameDesign.uk. Used consistently across all hero components, landing pages, and primary CTAs sitewide. Reflects the site's core promise: replacing guesswork and intuition-based design with rigorous, mathematically grounded tools and theory. Secondary tagline 'Design with Authority.' is retired and should not appear in new content.", "hero_headline_canonical": "Model It Before You Build It. — This headline synthesises the empirical rigour implied by 'Design with Authority' and the action-orientation of 'Start Building. Stop Guessing.' It positions the site as a modelling and simulation layer that precedes production, which is accurate to the toolset (calculators, probability distributions, progression curve models). It carries the punchy declarative fragment style consistent with the established voice, avoids credential-claiming, and creates productive tension by implying the reader's current workflow skips the modelling step. All hero components across index, tool pages, and landing pages should reference this canonical value. The two competing variants should be retired."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	f	2026-04-07 11:22:44.370823+00	2026-04-08 11:32:31.994344+00	content-gap-planner	f
19033adf-fa65-41bc-bee8-d6c904bd68fe	2a8ebf9c-20a2-4c39-b191-840b012371da	identity	{"team": [{"bio": "Over 30 years of engineering experience across startups, scale-ups, and enterprise systems. Built and operated worldsoccernews.com — one of the world's busiest sports sites, holding top search engine placement for highly competitive terms for over a decade. Former senior engineer at Bumble. Strong financial systems background. Designed this multi-agent orchestration framework from the conviction that many specialised AI agents collaborating through robust infrastructure outperform any single-model approach. The framework now coordinates 30+ agent types on Kubernetes and Kafka, managing thousands of concurrent agent instances in production across websites, data pipelines, and research systems.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "photo": "", "title": "Principal Consultant"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Leads a team of specialist research agents that investigate before anything gets built or published. Depending on the task, Archivist coordinates deep web research, source credibility verification, structured data extraction from industry registries, Companies House cross-referencing, and competitive analysis. Whether the job is grounding a content page in verified facts or building a dataset of 10,000 businesses with financial enrichment, Archivist's team ensures the output is sourced, attributed, and accurate.", "name": "Archivist", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Research"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Coordinates a team of specialist auditors that continuously monitor everything we deploy — websites, data pipelines, interactive tools, news feeds, and content accuracy. Each auditor focuses on a different dimension: structural integrity, content quality, design consistency, factual accuracy, and data pipeline health. Findings are classified by severity and routed to the right specialist for resolution. Full audit trails on every finding and fix.", "name": "Sentinel", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Quality Assurance"}, {"bio": "AI managing agent. Runs the ongoing improvement of every deployed system. Quartermaster coordinates maintenance cycles across a team of specialist agents — each responsible for a different concern: content freshness, tool health, navigation structure, news feed reliability, data quality, and deployment integrity. Every improvement cycle is observable and every change can be routed through human review before it takes effect. Systems get better between review cycles, with routine maintenance handled autonomously.", "name": "Quartermaster", "photo": "", "title": "Head of Operations"}], "tone": "professional yet approachable", "email": "agents@contactforsales.com", "phone": "+44 (0) 7934 524 911", "tagline": "Agile AI Agents: Move Swiftly into Digital Transformation with Grace and Precision", "industry": "AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services", "services": [{"name": "Automated Website Solutions", "description": "Get production-ready websites up and running in minutes with our AI-powered multi-agent systems. We handle secure, scalable hosting on Cloudflare, including automated builds, testing, and launches – removing the usual hurdles so you can focus on what matters."}, {"name": "Multi-Agent Systems", "description": "We design custom hierarchical agent setups to address your business challenges. Supporting a range of LLMs and models, these systems delegate tasks sensibly, collaborate in real time, and scale smoothly for effective automation."}, {"name": "Digital Transformation Strategy", "description": "Clear guidance to integrate AI and modern technology into your everyday operations. We work with you to build straightforward roadmaps for AI adoption, streamlining workflows, and staying agile in a fast-changing world."}, {"name": "Web Consultancy", "description": "Practical advice on modern web architectures, smart deployment, and useful AI integrations. We help your team build solid, forward-thinking web applications that focus on speed, security, and real innovation."}], "company_name": "AI Agent Orchestration", "about_summary": "AI Agent Orchestration builds production-grade multi-agent systems on proven infrastructure — Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres. We design hierarchical agent architectures that automate complex workflows, from automated website deployment to real-time agent collaboration. No demos. No slide decks. Working systems, deployed and running.", "site_metadata": "industry: AI infrastructure and enterprise software; target_audience: CTOs, engineering leads, and technology decision-makers at mid-to-large enterprises and scaling startups evaluating or deploying AI agent systems in production — secondary audience includes startup founders and business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable outcomes; tone: technical, direct, and practitioner-led — written by builders for builders, not advisory or consultative in register; purpose: lead generation for custom AI agent build engagements, supported by authoritative technical content that establishes credibility with engineering decision-makers", "leadership_team": [{"bio": "Peter is a technology strategist with strong enthusiasm for AI agent frameworks, modern web architecture, and automated systems. He leads our efforts in digital transformation, delivering agile innovation through effective multi-agent orchestration and quick deployments.", "name": "Peter Grenfell", "title": "Founder & Principal Consultant"}], "target_audience": "Primary: CTOs, VP Engineering, and engineering leads at mid-to-large enterprises (500+ employees) and Series B+ scaling startups who are evaluating or actively deploying AI agent systems in production. They prioritize reliability, observability, compliance, and real cost-of-failure analysis over theoretical AI potential. They are skeptical of hype, reward technical depth, and validate vendors by architecture quality and production track record. Secondary: startup founders and business leaders seeking measurable ROI from AI-driven automation, who defer to engineering leadership for technical validation.", "key_differentiators": "Our agile approach to AI orchestration\\nFast deployments (minutes instead of weeks)\\nSolid enterprise-level security and reliability\\nProven stack with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres\\nStrong expertise in hierarchical multi-agent systems\\nSpecial focus on web automation – with room to grow into other areas", "target_audience_tone_purpose": "Target Audience: CTOs, engineering leads, VP Engineering, and technically sophisticated startup founders evaluating production AI infrastructure. Secondary: forward-thinking business owners who understand technology investment. Tone: Direct, confident, and technically credible — written by builders for builders. No fluff, no vague consulting language. Purpose: Lead generation and consultation bookings for AI agent orchestration engagements, supported by demonstration of deep technical competence through case studies, tooling, and blog content.", "industry_audience_tone_purpose": "Industry: AI infrastructure and enterprise automation. Target Audience: CTOs, engineering leads, and operations directors at mid-market to enterprise companies, plus scaling startup founders evaluating production AI agent deployments. Tone: confident, direct, and technically credible — written by builders for builders, not by consultants for executives. Purpose: generate qualified inbound leads for custom multi-agent system design and production deployment engagements.", "target_audience_tone_and_conversion_goals": "Primary audience: CTOs, VP Engineering, and senior engineering leads at Series B+ startups and mid-to-large enterprises who are actively evaluating or deploying AI agent systems in production. Secondary audience: startup founders and technically-literate business leaders seeking measurable AI automation outcomes. Tone: technical, direct, and peer-to-peer — written by engineers who build real systems, not consultants who theorize. Avoid marketing fluff; lead with architecture decisions, production tradeoffs, and concrete outcomes. Primary conversion goal: discovery call or contact form submission. Secondary goal: blog content engagement and return visits that build trust before outreach.", "industry,target_audience,tone,messaging_pillars": "industry: AI consulting / agent orchestration / technology services. target_audience_primary: CTOs, VP Engineering, and engineering leads at mid-to-large enterprises and scaling startups who are evaluating or actively deploying AI agent systems in production — they are technical, skeptical of hype, and need production-grade answers not theoretical frameworks. target_audience_secondary: Startup founders and forward-thinking business leaders seeking practical AI-driven automation with measurable business outcomes. tone: Direct, technically credible, practitioner-first — written by engineers who ship real systems, not consultants who produce slide decks. No hype, no vague promises. Concrete stack references (Kubernetes, Kafka, Postgres), real failure modes, and honest trade-offs. messaging_pillars: (1) Production reality over proof-of-concept theater — we build systems that survive contact with real workloads. (2) Orchestration as a first-class engineering discipline, not an afterthought. (3) Stack-specific expertise — opinionated choices grounded in operational experience. (4) Measurable outcomes — agent systems justified by business impact, not novelty."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-04-07 13:51:23.305595+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
d927fd18-b898-497a-8ffe-eab0b5218270	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	mission_brief	{"text": "Spark is an AI-driven social platform where the world is the content and your take is the game.\\n\\nPositioning: Not another social app. A daily game powered by what is happening in the world. You don't post. You don't scroll. You play.\\n\\nTagline: TikTok is where you watch. Twitter is where you shout. Spark is where you play.\\n\\nKey differentiators:\\n- AI as game master and producer, never the performer — when something is funny or impressive, a human did it\\n- Opinion-first entry point — you need a take, not an idea\\n- Ephemeral challenges with permanent emergent reputation — disposable content, lasting identity\\n- Rooms not feeds — enter a space with energy, don't scroll a stream\\n- Arena (competitive takes) + Stage (creative showcase) dual modes\\n- Archetypes earned from behaviour, not self-reported — your profile emerges from how you engage\\n\\nTarget users:\\n- Primary: People with opinions on current trends but no platform that asks for them\\n- Secondary: Creators wanting skill showcase with built-in audience and niche discovery\\n- Tertiary: Curators and tastemakers — people who find things, not make things\\n\\nContent tone: interesting, slightly adult, competitive, aspirational, playful, game-like, energetic\\nNot: dark, gruesome, violent, corporate, generic social media, AI slop\\nAI role: Producer not performer. AI frames, scores, curates, synthesises. Never does humour, hot takes, sarcasm."}	domain-submitter	domain-submitter	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 09:49:01.387083+00	\N	domain-submitter	f
ed775aa8-cd8f-496f-81b9-50df11f4022b	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	roadmap	{"phases": {"v4_and_beyond": {"status": "speculative", "description": "Stage mode. Multi-format. Niche discovery. Monetisation."}, "v1_content_first": {"pages": [{"slug": "index", "purpose": "The product IS the landing page. Single provocation card filling screen. Text input beneath. Timer. No signup wall.", "priority": 1, "section_types": ["provocation-card", "lobby-grid", "brief-explanation", "gauntlet-cta"]}, {"slug": "provocations", "purpose": "Today's active provocations with AI takes. Each has shareable URL. SEO content. Card-based layout.", "priority": 2, "section_types": ["provocation-feed"]}, {"slug": "gauntlet", "purpose": "Daily Gauntlet — 5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. Client-side JS.", "priority": 3, "section_types": ["gauntlet-interface", "archetype-result-card"], "content_context": {"archetypes": [{"name": "The Surgeon", "tagline": "Precise, analytical, cuts to the core", "strengths": "Analytical speed, structural clarity, finding hidden flaws", "description": "Strips arguments to essential structure. Fast on logical frameworks."}, {"name": "The Wildcard", "tagline": "Unpredictable, highest remix rate", "strengths": "Creative leaps, remix ability, cross-domain thinking", "description": "Takes ideas in unexpected directions. Crosses domains freely."}, {"name": "The Oracle", "tagline": "Quiet but accurate, rare but impactful", "strengths": "Prediction accuracy, timing, selective engagement", "description": "Does not respond often but when they do it lands. Best prediction accuracy."}, {"name": "The Catalyst", "tagline": "Responses generate longest chains", "strengths": "Provocation, opening angles, generating momentum", "description": "Individual responses might not be best, but they spark others."}, {"name": "The Judge", "tagline": "Spectates, but reactions predict outcomes", "strengths": "Pattern recognition, taste, predictive judgement", "description": "Lives in the Gallery. Reaction pattern most predictive of final outcomes."}, {"name": "The Maker", "tagline": "Stage-dominant, consistent showcaser", "strengths": "Creative output, consistency, skill demonstration", "description": "Shows up with creations not opinions. Demonstrates skill."}, {"name": "The Scout", "tagline": "Identifies breakout creators early", "strengths": "Early identification, taste, discovery", "description": "The curator. Finds things others miss."}, {"name": "The Mentor", "tagline": "Breakdowns among most saved content", "strengths": "Teaching, explanation, knowledge sharing", "description": "Explanations are teaching material. Turns admiration into learning."}], "gauntlet_mechanics": "5 provocations mixing opinion and creation prompts. Scored on response speed, originality, consistency, topic preferences. Produces primary archetype with secondary tendencies. Shareable visual card."}}, {"slug": "about", "purpose": "What Spark is. Quick, energetic explanation. Game metaphor. Arena vs Stage. AI game master concept.", "priority": 4, "section_types": ["hero", "platform-comparison", "game-master-explanation", "gauntlet-cta"], "content_context": {"key_comparisons": {"vs_reddit": "Reddit: permanent, karma-hierarchical, dominated by early commenters. Spark: ephemeral, anonymised during play, scored on quality not timing.", "vs_tiktok": "TikTok: passive consumption, massive creator/consumer divide. Spark: opinion entry point, Gauntlet proves anyone can participate in 5 minutes.", "vs_twitter": "Twitter: shouting into a void. Spark: put in a room where engagement is guaranteed."}, "game_master_explanation": "AI does not try to be funny or clever. AI runs the game: finds what is interesting (scraping), frames it sharply (provocation), keeps score (reputation, archetypes), synthesises results (recaps). Humans bring wit and creativity. AI builds the arena."}}, {"slug": "archetypes", "purpose": "Archetype system explained. Each gets section with name, tagline, description, strengths. Shareable individual cards.", "priority": 5, "section_types": ["hero", "archetype-grid", "archetype-combinations"], "content_context": {"combination_examples": ["Surgeon-Oracle: Rarely speaks, but precisely targeted insight that predicts outcomes", "Wildcard-Catalyst: Unexpected ideas everyone wants to riff on", "Maker-Mentor: Creates consistently and teaches others to improve", "Scout-Judge: Does not create or opine, but most trusted taste on the platform"]}}], "status": "active", "hosting": "s3_static", "features": ["daily_provocation_generation_from_scraping", "ai_take_per_provocation", "shareable_provocation_cards", "daily_gauntlet_client_side", "archetype_generation_and_share_cards", "daily_static_regeneration"], "description": "Static S3 site. Provocations as SEO content. Daily Gauntlet as viral archetype quiz.", "design_direction": "Game energy, not corporate. Dark theme with vibrant accents. Cards, timers, energy indicators. Arena lobby feel. Mobile-first.", "success_criteria": {"daily_visitors": 50, "avg_session_seconds": 180, "gauntlet_completion_rate": 0.15}}, "v3_rooms_and_community": {"status": "speculative", "description": "Live challenge rooms. Arena mode. Chains. Duels. Reputation."}, "v2_sparring_and_interaction": {"status": "directional", "description": "AI sparring on provocations. User accounts. Live reactions."}}, "current_phase": "v1_content_first"}	domain-submitter	domain-submitter	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 09:49:02.028878+00	\N	domain-submitter	f
b1ef7082-acc6-42ec-97cd-d1ff683c953a	e1e22a7d-0552-405a-85b3-1b1e51384df5	roadmap_brief	{"text": "Current phase: v1_content_first\\nStatic S3 site. Provocations as SEO content. Daily Gauntlet as viral archetype quiz.\\nDesign: Game energy, not corporate. Dark theme with vibrant accents. Cards, timers, energy indicators. Arena lobby feel. Mobile-first.\\n\\nPages for this phase:\\n- index: The product IS the landing page. Single provocation card filling screen. Text input beneath. Timer. No signup wall.\\n  Sections: provocation-card, lobby-grid, brief-explanation, gauntlet-cta\\n- provocations: Today's active provocations with AI takes. Each has shareable URL. SEO content. Card-based layout.\\n  Sections: provocation-feed\\n- gauntlet: Daily Gauntlet — 5 provocations, 5 minutes, discover your archetype. Client-side JS. Produces shareable archetype card.\\n  Sections: gauntlet-interface, archetype-result-card\\n- about: What Spark is. Quick, energetic explanation. Game metaphor. Arena vs Stage. AI game master concept. How archetypes work.\\n  Sections: hero, platform-comparison, game-master-explanation, gauntlet-cta\\n- archetypes: Archetype system explained. Each gets section with name, tagline, description, strengths. Shareable individual cards.\\n  Sections: hero, archetype-grid, archetype-combinations\\n\\nFuture phases (not for building now):\\n- v2: AI sparring on provocations, user accounts, live reactions\\n- v3: Live challenge rooms, arena mode, chains, duels, reputation\\n- v4: Stage mode, monetisation, vertical integration"}	domain-submitter	domain-submitter	\N	\N	t	2026-04-02 09:49:07.805944+00	\N	domain-submitter	f
