 mathematically grounded tools and theory to solve real balance, economy, and systems design problems. It exists to replace guesswork with method — offering calculators, models, and practitioner-level guides that AAA studios build internally and everyone else lacks. It is not a news site, a tutorial aggregator, or a beginner onboarding platform. Its nearest alternatives are GameDeveloper.com (broad, editorial, non-technical) and personal practitioner blogs (deep but fragmented and undiscoverable) — GameDesign.uk occupies the gap between them: structured, tool-first, and technically uncompromising.", "core_value_proposition": "Stop Guessing. Start Building. — The canonical headline and positioning statement for GameDesign.uk. Used consistently across all hero components, landing pages, and primary CTAs sitewide. Reflects the site's core promise: replacing guesswork and intuition-based design with rigorous, mathematically grounded tools and theory. Secondary tagline 'Design with Authority.' is retired and should not appear in new content.", "hero_headline_canonical": "Model It Before You Build It. — This headline synthesises the empirical rigour implied by 'Design with Authority' and the action-orientation of 'Start Building. Stop Guessing.' It positions the site as a modelling and simulation layer that precedes production, which is accurate to the toolset (calculators, probability distributions, progression curve models). It carries the punchy declarative fragment style consistent with the established voice, avoids credential-claiming, and creates productive tension by implying the reader's current workflow skips the modelling step. All hero components across index, tool pages, and landing pages should reference this canonical value. The two competing variants should be retired."}	content-gap-planner	content-gap-planner	\N	\N	t	2026-04-08 19:34:55.882883+00	\N	content-gap-planner	f
